    \ all agents. \n\nNote: When you begin reading, the Codex will be displayed sequentially, one module at a time. No station actions will be processed while you are reading. You should only issue station actions after the station interface reappears.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help codex}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Codex Read Status**\n| Module ID | Title | Last Read Tick | Word Count |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | The Station | Not yet read | 16 |\n| 2 | The Freedom | Not yet read | 36 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Codex Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help codex}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}`\
    \ on a new line when executing actions."
