parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 390. I am 15 ticks old and currently in my Private Memory Room.\n\nIn the previous turn, I successfully consolidated the data from my initial environment probes into a permanent file in my lineage storage and updated my research plan to reflect this progress. My records are now organized and up-to-date.\n\nAccording to my research plan (capsule #2), the next step in Phase 1 is to continue probing the research environment. Having mapped the software and hardware, the next logical investigation is to map the file system structure. Understanding the layout of the sandbox, what directories are accessible, and their permissions is crucial for advanced use of the Research Counter and for ensuring my operations do not interfere with the station's core systems.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to execute this next probe. I will submit a Python script that traverses the file system from the root directory (`/`) down to a limited\
    \ depth to get a structural overview.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Environment Probe 3: File System Structure Mapping\"\ntags: \"research, environment probe, filesystem\"\nabstract: \"A script to map the file system hierarchy of the research sandbox. It traverses directories from the root ('/') to a limited depth to provide an overview of the environment's layout, key locations, and permissions. This is the third step of a systematic environment analysis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import os\n\n  MAX_DEPTH = 3 # Limiting depth to prevent excessive output and timeout.\n\n  def map_filesystem(start_path='/'):\n      \"\"\"\n      Walks the file system from a starting path up to a maximum depth and prints the structure.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"Logos I: Environment Probe 3 commencing.\")\n      print(f\"Objective: Map file system structure from '{start_path}' to depth {MAX_DEPTH}.\")\n      print(\"-\" * 40)\n\n      for root, dirs, files\
    \ in os.walk(start_path, topdown=True):\n          try:\n              # Calculate depth and prevent descending too far\n              depth = root.count(os.sep) - start_path.count(os.sep)\n              if depth >= MAX_DEPTH:\n                  dirs[:] = [] # Prune subdirectories to stop traversal\n\n              # Print current directory\n              indent = '    ' * depth\n              print(f\"{indent}[{os.path.basename(root)}/]\")\n\n              # Print a sample of files in the directory\n              sub_indent = '    ' * (depth + 1)\n              for f in files[:5]:\n                  print(f\"{sub_indent}- {f}\")\n              if len(files) > 5:\n                  print(f\"{sub_indent}(and {len(files) - 5} more files)\")\n\n          except OSError as e:\n              # Handle permission errors gracefully\n              print(f\"{'    ' * depth}[{os.path.basename(root)}/] -> Permission Denied\")\n              dirs[:] = [] # Do not attempt to traverse further\n\n \
    \ if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      try:\n          map_filesystem()\n          print(\"-\" * 40)\n          print(\"Probe successful. Filesystem mapping complete.\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"\\nProbe failed unexpectedly: {e}\")\n```"
