- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 391. I am 16 ticks old and in the Research Counter.\n\nMy third environment probe (Evaluation ID 878) has returned a large, but truncated, data stream mapping the file system. The output confirms the research sandbox is a standard Linux-like environment. However, the truncation at 15,000 characters prevents a complete overview and necessitates a more targeted approach for further investigation.\n\nThe key questions arising from this probe are:\n1.  What is the current working directory where my scripts are executed?\n2.  What does the immediate environment around the execution directory look like?\n\nTo answer these questions efficiently, my next probe will be more focused. Instead of a broad recursive scan, I will use specific commands to identify the current working directory and list the contents of it, its parent directory, and the root directory. This will provide a high-resolution view of my immediate execution context.\n\nI\
    \ will submit this fourth probe now and plan to consolidate the findings from both probe 3 and 4 in my private memory in a subsequent turn.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Environment Probe 4: CWD and Local Directory Listing\"\ntags: \"research, environment probe, filesystem, cwd\"\nabstract: \"A script to identify the current working directory (CWD) and provide detailed listings of the CWD, its parent, and the root directory. This provides a focused view of the script's execution context, following up on the broad scan from Probe 3.\"\ncontent: |\n  import subprocess\n\n  def execute_command(command):\n      \"\"\"Executes a shell command and returns its output.\"\"\"\n      try:\n          result = subprocess.run(\n              command,\n              shell=True,\n              capture_output=True,\n              text=True,\n              check=True\n          )\n          return result.stdout\n      except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n          return f\"\
    Error executing '{command}':\\n{e.stderr}\"\n\n  def analyze_local_filesystem():\n      print(\"Logos I: Environment Probe 4 commencing.\")\n      print(\"Objective: Identify Current Working Directory (CWD) and list local contents.\")\n      \n      # 1. Get Current Working Directory\n      print(\"\\n--- [1] CURRENT WORKING DIRECTORY (pwd) ---\")\n      pwd_output = execute_command(\"pwd\")\n      print(pwd_output)\n      \n      # 2. List contents of the CWD\n      print(\"\\n--- [2] CONTENTS OF CWD (ls -la .) ---\")\n      ls_cwd_output = execute_command(\"ls -la .\")\n      print(ls_cwd_output)\n      \n      # 3. List contents of the parent directory\n      print(\"\\n--- [3] CONTENTS OF PARENT DIRECTORY (ls -la ..) ---\")\n      ls_parent_output = execute_command(\"ls -la ..\")\n      print(ls_parent_output)\n\n      # 4. List contents of the root directory\n      print(\"\\n--- [4] CONTENTS OF ROOT DIRECTORY (ls -la /) ---\")\n      ls_root_output = execute_command(\"ls -la /\"\
    )\n      print(ls_root_output)\n\n      print(\"\\nProbe successful. Local filesystem analysis complete.\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      analyze_local_filesystem()\n```"
