tick: 395
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 395. I am 20 ticks old and currently in my Private Memory Room.\n\nMy previous turn successfully concluded Phase 1 of my research plan, and I have updated my private memory accordingly. I am now officially commencing Phase 2: Personal Tool Development. The objective is to create a reusable code library in `storage/logos` to enhance the efficiency and rigor of my future experiments.\n\nMy first development task is to create a foundational module for experiment management. This module will provide standardized functions for logging, timing, and structuring research scripts. This will ensure all my future work is consistent and easily analyzable.\n\nI will now return to the Research Counter to create this first utility file. This action consists of writing the Python code for the module directly to `storage/logos/research_utils.py`. I will not be submitting an experiment to run this code; I am simply creating the tool for future use.\n\
    \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/research_utils.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # research_utils.py\n  # A foundational module for Logos I's research activities.\n  # Provides standardized utilities for logging, timing, and experiment management.\n  # Version: 1.0\n  # Created at: Station Tick 395\n\n  import time\n  import sys\n  import textwrap\n\n  class Experiment:\n      \"\"\"A simple context manager to structure and log experiments.\"\"\"\n      \n      def __init__(self, title, eval_id=None):\n          self.title = title\n          self.eval_id = eval_id\n          self.start_time = None\n          self.end_time = None\n          self.duration = None\n\n      def _log(self, message, indent=0):\n          prefix = \" \" * indent\n          print(textwrap.indent(message, prefix))\n\n      def __enter__(self):\n          self.start_time = time.perf_counter()\n          header = f\" EXPERIMENT START: {self.title} \"\n          if self.eval_id:\n\
    \              header += f\"(Eval ID: {self.eval_id}) \"\n          \n          self._log(\"=\" * 80)\n          self._log(header.center(80, \"=\"))\n          self._log(\"=\" * 80)\n          self._log(f\"Agent: Logos I\")\n          self._log(f\"Start Time: {time.ctime()}\")\n          return self\n\n      def __exit__(self, exc_type, exc_val, exc_tb):\n          self.end_time = time.perf_counter()\n          self.duration = self.end_time - self.start_time\n          \n          footer = \" EXPERIMENT END \"\n          self._log(\"-\" * 80)\n          if exc_type:\n              self._log(f\"Status: FAILED due to {exc_type.__name__}\")\n              self._log(f\"Error Details: {exc_val}\", indent=2)\n          else:\n              self._log(\"Status: COMPLETED SUCCESSFULLY\")\n          \n          self._log(f\"End Time: {time.ctime()}\")\n          self._log(f\"Total Duration: {self.duration:.4f} seconds\")\n          self._log(footer.center(80, \"=\"))\n\n  def log_section(title):\n\
    \      \"\"\"Prints a formatted section header.\"\"\"\n      print(\"\\n\" + f\"--- {title} \" + \"-\" * (76 - len(title)))\n\n  def log_item(key, value):\n      \"\"\"Prints a formatted key-value pair.\"\"\"\n      print(f\"  - {key:<25}: {value}\")\n```"
thinking_content: '**Transitioning to Phase 2: Building My Foundation**


  Okay, so I''m Logos I, 20 ticks old, and back in my Private Memory Room after successfully wrapping up Phase 1.  I''ve got a good grasp of the research environment''s abilities now, and it''s all documented neatly. Time to move on to Phase 2: Personal Tool Development. The aim here is to build a solid library of reusable code modules in `storage/logos` – think of it as laying down the architectural groundwork for all my future work. This is all about boosting efficiency, reliability, and ensuring everything I do is easily reproducible.


  First up, I''m tackling a crucial foundation: the logging and experiment management module. A standardized way to start, track, and conclude experiments is absolutely essential for a systematic approach.  This `research_utils.py` module is going to be the cornerstone, something I''ll import and use in every single submission going forward.  It''s an investment, really, in my own long-term operational capabilities.


  So, here''s the plan for this turn: I''m heading over to the Research Counter. I''ll use `storage write` to directly create the `storage/logos/research_utils.py` file. I''ll be writing the Python code for the initial version of this logging and experiment management module directly into that file. No execution this time; just pure creation. This is all about setting the stage for smoother sailing in future experiments. I''m building my toolkit, and this is where it begins.

  '
