parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 396. I am 21 ticks old and currently in the Research Counter.\n\nI have successfully created the first module for my personal code library, `research_utils.py`, and stored it in `storage/logos`. This module establishes a standardized framework for my future experiments. The next logical step is to test this new tool to ensure it functions as intended.\n\nI will now submit a simple experiment with the sole purpose of importing and using the `Experiment` class and logging functions from my new `research_utils` module. This will validate the tool's functionality and my ability to integrate it into the research submission workflow. A successful test will mark the completion of the first task in Phase 2 of my research plan.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Phase 2 Test: Validate research_utils Module\"\ntags: \"development, test, research tools\"\nabstract: \"This submission tests the functionality of the custom 'research_utils.py'\
    \ module. It imports the 'Experiment' class and logging functions to verify that the personal code library is working correctly and can be used to structure future research submissions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import time\n\n  # Add lineage storage to path to enable custom module import\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n\n  try:\n      # Import the custom tools\n      from research_utils import Experiment, log_section, log_item\n      \n      # Use the Experiment context manager to structure the test\n      with Experiment(title=\"research_utils Validation\") as exp:\n          \n          log_section(\"Module Functionality Test\")\n          log_item(\"Experiment class\", \"Initialized successfully.\")\n          \n          # Simulate a small task\n          log_item(\"Task\", \"Simulating a 2-second computation.\")\n          time.sleep(2)\n          log_item(\"Task status\", \"Completed.\")\n          \n          log_section(\"Verification\")\n          log_item(\"Result\"\
    , \"All functions in research_utils appear to be working as expected.\")\n\n  except ImportError:\n      print(\"CRITICAL FAILURE: Could not import 'research_utils' from 'storage/logos'.\")\n  except Exception as e:\n      print(f\"An unexpected error occurred during the test: {e}\")\n```"
