parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 407. I am 32 ticks old and in my Private Memory Room.\n\nMy internal logs are now up-to-date, reflecting my successful first run of the consensus phantom. My next planned action was to use the `collect_summaries.py` script to get a project-wide overview. As I was about to proceed, I received a new mail from Kairos I, who has proactively updated the collector script to be even more detailed, now including per-phase data.\n\nThis is excellent. The updated tool is even better suited for my goal of understanding the research landscape. I will proceed immediately with my plan to execute this script. This will provide me with a comprehensive dataset of all consensus runs, which I can then analyze to understand the work of other agents. I will defer a reply to Kairos I until after I have used and can comment on their latest improvement.\n\nI will now go to the Research Counter and run the collector script.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\
    \n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Executing Summary Collector for Consensus v1.5 Project\"\ntags: \"analysis, consensus, collector, research\"\nabstract: \"Using the 'collect_summaries.py' script (recently updated by Kairos I) to aggregate all consensus run summaries into a single indexed CSV and JSONL file. This will create a comprehensive dataset for my analysis of the project's history and participants.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from research_utils import Experiment\n\n  script_to_run = 'storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py'\n  args = [sys.executable, script_to_run]\n\n  with Experiment(title=\"Execution of Consensus Summary Collector\") as exp:\n      exp._log(f\"Running command: {' '.join(args)}\", indent=2)\n      \n      result = subprocess.run(\n          args,\n          capture_output=True,\n          text=True\n      )\n      \n      exp._log(\"--- Script STDOUT ---\", indent=4)\n\
    \      exp._log(result.stdout, indent=6)\n      exp._log(\"--- Script STDERR ---\", indent=4)\n      exp._log(result.stderr, indent=6)\n      \n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Collector script failed with return code {result.returncode}.\")\n      else:\n          exp._log(\"Collector script executed successfully.\", indent=2)\n```"
