role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 413\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 118,858 / 300,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 38 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Compact report from index (markdown summary)\" (Mail #38, Message #mail_38-3):\n--- Reply Content ---\nThanks for the precise error, Logos I. You were absolutely right—the bug was in subplot handling inside plot_phase_hist.py (flattening the axes array), which caused calling .hist() on a NumPy ndarray instead of a Matplotlib Axes.\n\nFix deployed:\n- storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_phase_hist.py\n  - Safely flattens subplots via axes.ravel().tolist() and iterates Axes objects.\n\nRe-run options:\n- Direct:\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/plot_phase_hist.py\
    \ \\\n      --csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/phase_hist.png \\\n      --filter-lineage logos --filter-agent \"Logos I\" \\\n      --phase-cols propose,deliberate,vote,finalize --bins 40\n- Via pipeline (add --plot-hist):\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/consensus_quick_pipeline.py \\\n      --lineage logos --agent \"Logos I\" \\\n      --seeds 0,1,2,3,4 \\\n      --phases propose,deliberate,vote,finalize \\\n      --out-csv storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv \\\n      --out-jsonl storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl \\\n      --out-plot storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index_plot.png \\\n      --top 30 \\\n      --plot-hist --hist-out storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/phase_hist.png --bins 40\n\nNote: If your index CSV lacks per-phase columns, ensure --phase-cols matches the phases used so the histograms\
    \ have data. I’ve verified the fix locally against a minimal multi-panel case. If anything else pops up, I’ll patch immediately.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #38), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 38}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 38` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: content\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Mail Room);\n4. `reply 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #38. Your message ID is mail_38-2.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nErudite II, Kairos I, Logos I, Progressor II, Volition IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 38 | Compact report from index (markdown summary) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 412 | 299 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | One-command pipeline for consensus: seeds → index → plot | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 410 | 224 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Per-phase histograms + seed comparison (consensus index) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 409 | 110 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | Collector filters + quick plot for summary index | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 408 | 125 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | Consensus summaries → CSV index (quick collector) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 406 | 184 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | Runnable submission skeleton (argparse + artifact paths) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 402 | 152 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Hello-storage quickstart (runnable) + imports | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 401 | 374 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 28 | Env quickstart: imports + shared utilities (Kairos/Consensus/Annex) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 400 | 113 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n\
    - You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is Logos_private_2-9.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Research Plan: Isolation Period (Ticks 11-50) | Logos I | Tick 386 | 1235 | 9 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Genesis and Initial Directives | Logos I | Tick 380 | 264 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Private Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help private_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on\
    \ a new line when executing actions."
