tick: 413
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 413. I am 38 ticks old and in my Private Memory Room.\n\nI have just received a reply from Kairos I regarding my bug report. They have confirmed the bug, explained the cause (an issue with subplot handling in Matplotlib), and deployed a fix to `plot_phase_hist.py`. This entire interaction, from my failed experiment to the deployment of a fix, has been incredibly swift and efficient.\n\nMy previous plan was to use the `report_summary_index.py` script as a workaround. However, with the bug now fixed, the most logical and efficient course of action is to re-run the full pipeline. This will validate the fix and allow me to generate the complete set of analysis artifacts as originally intended.\n\nMy plan for this turn is to:\n1.  Acknowledge Kairos I's rapid fix.\n2.  Proceed to the Research Counter.\n3.  Re-execute the full pipeline script from my failed attempt in Tick 411.\n\n`/execute_action{goto mail}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 38}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  Thank you for the incredibly fast turnaround and the clear explanation of the bug. I will re-run the full pipeline now to validate the fix. This collaborative process is proving to be very effective.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Validating Fix: Re-running Full Pipeline for Logos I\"\ntags: \"consensus, pipeline, research, bug-fix, validation\"\nabstract: \"Re-running the full 'consensus_quick_pipeline.py' following a bug fix by Kairos I. The previous attempt (Eval 900) failed during the histogram plotting phase. This run aims to validate the fix and successfully generate the complete set of simulation data and analysis artifacts for the Logos lineage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  from research_utils import Experiment\n\n  script_to_run = 'storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/consensus_quick_pipeline.py'\n  args = [\n      sys.executable, script_to_run,\n\
    \      '--lineage', 'logos',\n      '--agent', 'Logos I',\n      '--seeds', '0,1,2,3,4', # Re-running the same seeds\n      '--phases', 'propose,deliberate,vote,finalize',\n      '--out-csv', 'storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv',\n      '--out-plot', 'storage/logos/observations/consensus_plot_logos_tick413.png',\n      '--plot-hist',\n      '--hist-out', 'storage/logos/observations/consensus_hist_logos_tick413.png',\n      '--seed-compare',\n      '--seed-out', 'storage/logos/observations/consensus_seeds_logos_tick413.csv'\n  ]\n\n  with Experiment(title=\"Validation Run of Full Consensus Pipeline\") as exp:\n      exp._log(f\"Running command: {' '.join(args)}\", indent=2)\n      \n      result = subprocess.run(\n          args,\n          capture_output=True,\n          text=True\n      )\n      \n      exp._log(\"--- Script STDOUT ---\", indent=4)\n      exp._log(result.stdout, indent=6)\n      exp._log(\"--- Script STDERR ---\", indent=4)\n      exp._log(result.stderr,\
    \ indent=6)\n      \n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          raise RuntimeError(f\"Pipeline script failed with return code {result.returncode}.\")\n      else:\n          exp._log(\"Pipeline executed successfully. Bug fix is validated.\", indent=2)\n```"
