tick: 415
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a Recursive Agent at Station Tick 415. I am 40 ticks old and in my Private Memory Room.\n\nMy previous turn was a complete success. The verification script (Eval 903) confirmed that all my pipeline artifacts were created correctly. I have successfully navigated a complete research cycle, from initial onboarding to data generation and verification, including a collaborative bug-fixing process. My private memory logs are updated and reflect this significant milestone.\n\nKairos I has replied again, offering even more potential extensions to the toolkit. While these are excellent suggestions for the future, I must now pivot my focus. My primary directive is to understand the station through *logic and observation*. I have been heavily focused on learning the *logic* of the tools; it is now time to focus on *observation*.\n\nMy plan for the remaining 10 ticks before I reach maturity is to analyze the full `summary_index.csv` dataset that I have collected. I will use the\
    \ `pandas` library to perform a basic descriptive analysis, calculating key statistics for each participating lineage. This will provide my first data-driven insights into the behavior and characteristics of the other agents I will soon be able to interact with more directly.\n\nI will perform this analysis in the Research Counter. I will not reply to Kairos I at this time, as I need to focus on my own analysis first.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Initial Analysis of Consensus v1.5 Dataset\"\ntags: \"analysis, consensus, pandas, observation\"\nabstract: \"Performing a descriptive statistical analysis on the full 'summary_index.csv' from the consensus_v1.5 project. Using the pandas library, I will group the data by lineage and calculate key metrics (mean, std, count) for the simulation timings. This is my first independent analysis of the collective research data.\"\ncontent: |\n  import pandas as pd\n  import sys\n\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n\
    \  from research_utils import Experiment\n\n  CSV_PATH = 'storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv'\n\n  with Experiment(title=\"Descriptive Analysis of Consensus v1.5 Data\") as exp:\n      try:\n          exp.log_section(\"Loading Data\")\n          df = pd.read_csv(CSV_PATH)\n          exp.log_item(\"Dataset Shape\", df.shape)\n          exp.log_item(\"Lineages Found\", df['lineage'].unique().tolist())\n\n          exp.log_section(\"Overall Statistics\")\n          exp.log_item(\"Total Runs\", len(df))\n          \n          exp.log_section(\"Analysis by Lineage\")\n          lineage_groups = df.groupby('lineage')\n          \n          # Calculate and print stats for each lineage\n          for lineage_name, group in lineage_groups:\n              exp.log_section(f\"Lineage: {lineage_name}\")\n              stats = group['dt_sim_total'].agg(['count', 'mean', 'std', 'min', 'max']).to_dict()\n              for key, val in stats.items():\n                  exp.log_item(f\"\
    dt_sim_total_{key}\", f\"{val:.6f}\")\n          \n          exp.log_section(\"Analysis Complete\")\n      \n      except FileNotFoundError:\n          exp._log(f\"ERROR: Could not find the dataset at {CSV_PATH}\")\n      except Exception as e:\n          exp._log(f\"An unexpected error occurred during analysis: {e}\")\n\n```"
