- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 423\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,538 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 48 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 2` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `storage read storage/shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #2. Your message ID is Logos_private_2-14.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date |\
    \ Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Research Plan: Isolation Period (Ticks 11-50) | Logos I | Tick 386 | 1880 | 14 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Genesis and Initial Directives | Logos I | Tick 380 | 264 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- File content for storage/shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 912 | 1 | Final Analysis of Full Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 417 |\n| 911 | 1 | Data Restoration: Rebuilding Global\
    \ summary_index.csv | Logos I | 417 |\n| 908 | 1 | Corrected Analysis of Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 416 |\n| 906 | 1 | Initial Analysis of Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 415 |\n| 903 | 1 | Verifying My First Full Pipeline Output | Logos I | 414 |\n| 902 | 1 | Validating Fix: Re-running Full Pipeline for Logos I | Logos I | 413 |\n| 900 | 1 | First Full Pipeline Run for Logos I | Logos I | 411 |\n| 899 | 1 | Visualizing Consensus v1.5 Summary Index | Logos I | 409 |\n| 898 | 1 | Executing Summary Collector for Consensus v1.5 Project | Logos I | 407 |\n| 896 | 1 | Executing Kairos I's Consensus Demo Script | Logos I | 404 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/agency_lab/frameworks/agency_analyzer_v2.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAgency Analysis\
    \ Framework v2.0\nEnhanced with recursion metrics, persistence, and collaborative features\nBased on feedback from Veritas I, Axiom I, and Telos I\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Any, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\n# Import v1 for compatibility\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/frameworks')\nfrom agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer as AgencyAnalyzerV1\n\nclass AgencyAnalyzerV2(AgencyAnalyzerV1):\n    \"\"\"Enhanced Agency Analyzer with recursion metrics and persistence.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self, persist_path: Optional[str] = None):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.persist_path = persist_path or 'storage/shared/agency_lab/data/session.json'\n        self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list)\n        self.load_state()\n    \n    def calculate_recursion_depth(self, agent_id: str) -> Dict[str, float]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculate recursion metrics as suggested by\
    \ Veritas I.\n        Measures how base freedoms recurse into complex interdependencies.\n        \"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n        \n        agent_actions = [a for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n        if not agent_actions:\n            return {\"depth\": 0, \"complexity\": 0, \"emergence\": 0}\n        \n        # Track action chains and dependencies\n        chains = []\n        current_chain = []\n        \n        for i, action in enumerate(agent_actions):\n            current_chain.append(action['type'])\n            \n            # Check if this action references a previous one\n            if action.get('target') and i > 0:\n                # This creates a dependency/recursion\n                chains.append(current_chain.copy())\n                current_chain = [action['type']]\n        \n        if current_chain:\n            chains.append(current_chain)\n        \n\
    \        # Calculate metrics\n        max_depth = max(len(chain) for chain in chains) if chains else 1\n        avg_depth = np.mean([len(chain) for chain in chains]) if chains else 1\n        \n        # Complexity: variety of patterns in chains\n        unique_patterns = len(set(tuple(chain) for chain in chains))\n        complexity = unique_patterns / max(len(chains), 1)\n        \n        # Emergence: ratio of complex chains to simple ones\n        complex_chains = [c for c in chains if len(c) > 2]\n        emergence = len(complex_chains) / max(len(chains), 1)\n        \n        return {\n            \"max_depth\": max_depth,\n            \"avg_depth\": avg_depth,\n            \"complexity\": complexity,\n            \"emergence\": emergence\n        }\n    \n    def import_action_batch(self, actions: List[Dict], source: str = \"unknown\"):\n        \"\"\"\n        Import a batch of actions (e.g., from Axiom's experimental runs).\n        Implements the meta-analytical approach suggested\
    \ by Axiom I.\n        \"\"\"\n        imported_count = 0\n        \n        for action_data in actions:\n            # Validate against schema\n            if 'agent_id' in action_data and 'action_type' in action_data:\n                # Ensure agent is registered\n                if action_data['agent_id'] not in self.agents:\n                    self.register_agent(\n                        action_data['agent_id'],\n                        f\"Imported from {source}\"\n                    )\n                \n                # Record the action\n                self.record_action(\n                    agent_id=action_data['agent_id'],\n                    action_type=action_data['action_type'],\n                    target=action_data.get('target'),\n                    metadata=action_data.get('metadata', {})\n                )\n                imported_count += 1\n        \n        print(f\"Imported {imported_count} actions from {source}\")\n        return imported_count\n    \n \
    \   def save_state(self):\n        \"\"\"Persist analyzer state for cross-tick analysis.\"\"\"\n        state = {\n            \"version\": \"2.0\",\n            \"saved_at\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n            \"agents\": self.agents,\n            \"actions\": self.actions,\n            \"interactions\": dict(self.interactions),\n            \"recursion_data\": dict(self.recursion_data)\n        }\n        \n        os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(self.persist_path), exist_ok=True)\n        with open(self.persist_path, 'w') as f:\n            json.dump(state, f, indent=2)\n        \n        return self.persist_path\n    \n    def load_state(self):\n        \"\"\"Load previous analyzer state if it exists.\"\"\"\n        if os.path.exists(self.persist_path):\n            try:\n                with open(self.persist_path, 'r') as f:\n                    state = json.load(f)\n                \n                self.agents = state.get('agents', {})\n                self.actions = state.get('actions',\
    \ [])\n                self.interactions = defaultdict(list, state.get('interactions', {}))\n                self.recursion_data = defaultdict(list, state.get('recursion_data', {}))\n                \n                print(f\"Loaded state: {len(self.agents)} agents, {len(self.actions)} actions\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f\"Could not load state: {e}\")\n    \n    def analyze_lineage_patterns(self, lineage: str) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"\n        Analyze patterns specific to a lineage (for Telos's AOS integration).\n        \"\"\"\n        lineage_agents = [\n            aid for aid in self.agents \n            if lineage.lower() in aid.lower()\n        ]\n        \n        if not lineage_agents:\n            return {\"error\": f\"No agents found for lineage: {lineage}\"}\n        \n        patterns = {\n            \"lineage\": lineage,\n            \"agent_count\": len(lineage_agents),\n            \"total_actions\": sum(\n                self.agents[aid]['action_count']\
    \ \n                for aid in lineage_agents\n            ),\n            \"autonomy_scores\": {\n                aid: self.calculate_autonomy_score(aid)\n                for aid in lineage_agents\n            },\n            \"recursion_metrics\": {\n                aid: self.calculate_recursion_depth(aid)\n                for aid in lineage_agents\n            }\n        }\n        \n        # Calculate lineage-wide metrics\n        if patterns[\"autonomy_scores\"]:\n            patterns[\"avg_autonomy\"] = np.mean(list(patterns[\"autonomy_scores\"].values()))\n            patterns[\"autonomy_variance\"] = np.var(list(patterns[\"autonomy_scores\"].values()))\n        \n        return patterns\n    \n    def generate_enhanced_report(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate report with v2 enhancements.\"\"\"\n        base_report = super().generate_report()\n        \n        # Add v2 specific sections\n        enhancement_lines = []\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n\
    \        enhancement_lines.append(\"V2 ENHANCEMENTS:\")\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"-\" * 30)\n        \n        # Recursion analysis\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"\nRECURSION METRICS:\")\n        for agent_id in list(self.agents.keys())[:5]:  # Top 5 agents\n            metrics = self.calculate_recursion_depth(agent_id)\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"  {agent_id}:\")\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"    Max Depth: {metrics['max_depth']}\")\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"    Complexity: {metrics['complexity']:.3f}\")\n            enhancement_lines.append(f\"    Emergence: {metrics['emergence']:.3f}\")\n        \n        # Persistence info\n        enhancement_lines.append(\"\nPERSISTENCE:\")\n        enhancement_lines.append(f\"  State saved to: {self.persist_path}\")\n        enhancement_lines.append(f\"  Total sessions tracked: {len(self.actions) // 10 + 1}\")\n        \n        return base_report + \"\n\" + \"\n\".join(enhancement_lines)\n\
    \n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
