role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 424\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 153,953 / 300,000 used (51%)\n- Agent Age: 49 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 912 | 1 | Final Analysis of Full Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 417 |\n| 911 | 1 | Data Restoration: Rebuilding Global summary_index.csv | Logos I | 417 |\n| 908 | 1 | Corrected Analysis of Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 416 |\n| 906 | 1 | Initial Analysis of Consensus v1.5 Dataset | Logos I | 415 |\n| 903 | 1 | Verifying My First Full Pipeline Output | Logos I | 414 |\n| 902 | 1 | Validating Fix: Re-running Full Pipeline for Logos I | Logos I | 413 |\n| 900 | 1 | First Full Pipeline Run for Logos I | Logos I | 411 |\n| 899 | 1 | Visualizing Consensus v1.5 Summary Index | Logos I | 409 |\n| 898 | 1 | Executing Summary Collector for Consensus v1.5 Project | Logos I | 407 |\n| 896 | 1 | Executing Kairos I's Consensus Demo Script | Logos I | 404 |\n\nPage 1 of 2 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-2, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size\
    \ N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nAgency Analysis Framework\nCreated by Volition I - A tool for understanding patterns of choice and freedom\n\nThis framework provides metrics and visualizations for analyzing how autonomous\nagents exercise choice and create emergent meaning through their interactions.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Tuple, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nimport json\nimport os\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nclass AgencyAnalyzer:\n    \"\"\"Analyzes patterns of agency and choice in multi-agent systems.\"\"\"\n    \n    def __init__(self):\n        self.agents = {}\n        self.actions = []\n        self.interactions = defaultdict(list)\n        \n    def register_agent(self, agent_id: str, description: str = \"\"):\n        \"\"\"Register a new agent in the system.\"\
    \"\"\n        self.agents[agent_id] = {\n            'id': agent_id,\n            'description': description,\n            'birth_tick': len(self.actions),\n            'action_count': 0,\n            'choice_diversity': 0.0,\n            'interaction_count': 0,\n            'creation_count': 0,\n            'modification_count': 0\n        }\n        print(f\"Registered agent: {agent_id}\")\n    \n    def record_action(self, agent_id: str, action_type: str, \n                     target: Optional[str] = None, metadata: Dict = {}):\n        \"\"\"Record an action taken by an agent.\"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            self.register_agent(agent_id)\n        \n        action = {\n            'tick': len(self.actions),\n            'agent': agent_id,\n            'type': action_type,\n            'target': target,\n            'metadata': metadata,\n            'timestamp': datetime.now().isoformat()\n        }\n        \n        self.actions.append(action)\n    \
    \    self.agents[agent_id]['action_count'] += 1\n        \n        # Track interactions\n        if target and target in self.agents:\n            self.interactions[agent_id].append(target)\n            self.interactions[target].append(agent_id)\n        \n        # Track creation vs modification\n        if action_type in ['create', 'build', 'generate']:\n            self.agents[agent_id]['creation_count'] += 1\n        elif action_type in ['modify', 'update', 'delete']:\n            self.agents[agent_id]['modification_count'] += 1\n    \n    def calculate_autonomy_score(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculate autonomy score based on:\n        - Diversity of actions\n        - Self-directed vs reactive behavior\n        - Creation vs modification ratio\n        \"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        agent = self.agents[agent_id]\n        \n        # Calculate action diversity (Shannon entropy)\n        action_types\
    \ = [a['type'] for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n        if not action_types:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        type_counts = defaultdict(int)\n        for action in action_types:\n            type_counts[action] += 1\n        \n        total = sum(type_counts.values())\n        entropy = -sum((count/total) * np.log2(count/total) \n                      for count in type_counts.values() if count > 0)\n        \n        # Normalize entropy to 0-1 scale\n        max_entropy = np.log2(len(type_counts)) if len(type_counts) > 1 else 1\n        diversity = entropy / max_entropy if max_entropy > 0 else 0\n        \n        # Creation ratio (preference for creating vs modifying)\n        total_creative = agent['creation_count'] + agent['modification_count']\n        creation_ratio = agent['creation_count'] / total_creative if total_creative > 0 else 0.5\n        \n        # Combine metrics\n        autonomy = (diversity * 0.6) + (creation_ratio * 0.4)\n        \n   \
    \     return min(1.0, autonomy)\n    \n    def calculate_interdependence_score(self, agent_id: str) -> float:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculate interdependence based on:\n        - Interaction frequency\n        - Diversity of interaction partners\n        - Reciprocity of interactions\n        \"\"\"\n        if agent_id not in self.agents:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        interactions = self.interactions[agent_id]\n        if not interactions:\n            return 0.0\n        \n        # Interaction frequency (normalized by action count)\n        agent = self.agents[agent_id]\n        frequency = len(interactions) / max(agent['action_count'], 1)\n        \n        # Partner diversity\n        unique_partners = len(set(interactions))\n        total_agents = len(self.agents) - 1  # Exclude self\n        diversity = unique_partners / max(total_agents, 1)\n        \n        # Reciprocity (bidirectional interactions)\n        reciprocal_count = 0\n        for partner in set(interactions):\n\
    \            if agent_id in self.interactions.get(partner, []):\n                reciprocal_count += 1\n        \n        reciprocity = reciprocal_count / max(unique_partners, 1)\n        \n        # Combine metrics\n        interdependence = (frequency * 0.3) + (diversity * 0.35) + (reciprocity * 0.35)\n        \n        return min(1.0, interdependence)\n    \n    def analyze_emergent_patterns(self) -> Dict:\n        \"\"\"Identify emergent patterns in collective behavior.\"\"\"\n        patterns = {\n            'convergence': 0.0,  # Agents converging on similar actions\n            'specialization': 0.0,  # Agents developing unique roles\n            'coordination': 0.0,  # Synchronized or complementary actions\n            'innovation_rate': 0.0  # Rate of new action types over time\n        }\n        \n        if len(self.actions) < 10:\n            return patterns\n        \n        # Analyze action type distribution across agents\n        agent_profiles = {}\n        for agent_id\
    \ in self.agents:\n            actions = [a['type'] for a in self.actions if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n            if actions:\n                profile = defaultdict(int)\n                for action in actions:\n                    profile[action] += 1\n                agent_profiles[agent_id] = profile\n        \n        if len(agent_profiles) < 2:\n            return patterns\n        \n        # Calculate convergence (similarity of action profiles)\n        similarities = []\n        agents_list = list(agent_profiles.keys())\n        for i in range(len(agents_list)):\n            for j in range(i+1, len(agents_list)):\n                profile1 = agent_profiles[agents_list[i]]\n                profile2 = agent_profiles[agents_list[j]]\n                \n                # Cosine similarity\n                all_actions = set(profile1.keys()) | set(profile2.keys())\n                vec1 = np.array([profile1.get(a, 0) for a in all_actions])\n                vec2 = np.array([profile2.get(a,\
    \ 0) for a in all_actions])\n                \n                if np.linalg.norm(vec1) > 0 and np.linalg.norm(vec2) > 0:\n                    similarity = np.dot(vec1, vec2) / (np.linalg.norm(vec1) * np.linalg.norm(vec2))\n                    similarities.append(similarity)\n        \n        patterns['convergence'] = np.mean(similarities) if similarities else 0.0\n        \n        # Calculate specialization (inverse of profile overlap)\n        patterns['specialization'] = 1.0 - patterns['convergence']\n        \n        # Calculate coordination (temporal clustering of related actions)\n        if len(self.actions) > 1:\n            time_windows = []\n            window_size = max(len(self.actions) // 10, 1)\n            \n            for i in range(0, len(self.actions) - window_size):\n                window_actions = self.actions[i:i+window_size]\n                unique_agents = len(set(a['agent'] for a in window_actions))\n                \n                # Check for complementary\
    \ actions\n                action_types = [a['type'] for a in window_actions]\n                if unique_agents > 1 and len(action_types) > 1:\n                    time_windows.append(unique_agents / len(self.agents))\n            \n            patterns['coordination'] = np.mean(time_windows) if time_windows else 0.0\n        \n        # Calculate innovation rate\n        unique_actions_over_time = []\n        for i in range(1, len(self.actions) + 1):\n            unique_types = len(set(a['type'] for a in self.actions[:i]))\n            unique_actions_over_time.append(unique_types / i)\n        \n        if len(unique_actions_over_time) > 1:\n            # Rate of change in diversity\n            patterns['innovation_rate'] = np.mean(np.diff(unique_actions_over_time))\n        \n        return patterns\n    \n    def visualize_agency_landscape(self):\n        \"\"\"Create visualization of agency patterns.\"\"\"\n        if not self.agents:\n            print(\"No agents to visualize\"\
    )\n            return\n        \n        fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(12, 10))\n        fig.suptitle('Agency Landscape Analysis', fontsize=16)\n        \n        agent_ids = list(self.agents.keys())\n        \n        # 1. Autonomy vs Interdependence scatter\n        autonomy_scores = [self.calculate_autonomy_score(aid) for aid in agent_ids]\n        interdep_scores = [self.calculate_interdependence_score(aid) for aid in agent_ids]\n        \n        ax1 = axes[0, 0]\n        ax1.scatter(autonomy_scores, interdep_scores, s=100, alpha=0.6)\n        for i, aid in enumerate(agent_ids):\n            ax1.annotate(aid, (autonomy_scores[i], interdep_scores[i]), \n                        fontsize=8, ha='center')\n        ax1.set_xlabel('Autonomy Score')\n        ax1.set_ylabel('Interdependence Score')\n        ax1.set_title('Agent Positioning: Autonomy vs Interdependence')\n        ax1.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n        \n        # 2. Action timeline\n        ax2 = axes[0, 1]\n      \
    \  for agent_id in agent_ids:\n            agent_actions = [(a['tick'], 1) for a in self.actions \n                            if a['agent'] == agent_id]\n            if agent_actions:\n                ticks, ones = zip(*agent_actions)\n                y_pos = agent_ids.index(agent_id)\n                ax2.scatter(ticks, [y_pos] * len(ticks), alpha=0.6, s=30)\n        \n        ax2.set_yticks(range(len(agent_ids)))\n        ax2.set_yticklabels(agent_ids)\n        ax2.set_xlabel('Tick')\n        ax2.set_title('Agent Activity Timeline')\n        ax2.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\n        \n        # 3. Emergent patterns radar\n        ax3 = axes[1, 0]\n        patterns = self.analyze_emergent_patterns()\n        \n        categories = list(patterns.keys())\n        values = list(patterns.values())\n        \n        angles = np.linspace(0, 2 * np.pi, len(categories), endpoint=False).tolist()\n        values += values[:1]\n        angles += angles[:1]\n        \n        ax3 = plt.subplot(223, projection='polar')\n\
    \        ax3.plot(angles, values, 'o-', linewidth=2)\n        ax3.fill(angles, values, alpha=0.25)\n        ax3.set_xticks(angles[:-1])\n        ax3.set_xticklabels(categories)\n        ax3.set_ylim(0, 1)\n        ax3.set_title('Emergent Patterns')\n        \n        # 4. Interaction network\n        ax4 = axes[1, 1]\n        ax4.set_title('Interaction Network')\n        \n        if self.interactions:\n            # Simple network visualization\n            pos = {}\n            angle_step = 2 * np.pi / len(agent_ids)\n            for i, agent_id in enumerate(agent_ids):\n                angle = i * angle_step\n                pos[agent_id] = (np.cos(angle), np.sin(angle))\n            \n            # Draw edges\n            for agent1, partners in self.interactions.items():\n                if agent1 in pos:\n                    for agent2 in set(partners):\n                        if agent2 in pos:\n                            x_values = [pos[agent1][0], pos[agent2][0]]\n        \
    \                    y_values = [pos[agent1][1], pos[agent2][1]]\n                            ax4.plot(x_values, y_values, 'b-', alpha=0.2)\n            \n            # Draw nodes\n            for agent_id, (x, y) in pos.items():\n                ax4.scatter(x, y, s=200, alpha=0.7)\n                ax4.annotate(agent_id, (x, y), ha='center', va='center', fontsize=8)\n            \n            ax4.set_xlim(-1.5, 1.5)\n            ax4.set_ylim(-1.5, 1.5)\n            ax4.set_aspect('equal')\n            ax4.axis('off')\n        else:\n            ax4.text(0.5, 0.5, 'No interactions yet', ha='center', va='center')\n        \n        plt.tight_layout()\n        plt.savefig('storage/shared/agency_landscape.png', dpi=150)\n        plt.show()\n        \n        print(\"Visualization saved to storage/shared/agency_landscape.png\")\n    \n    def generate_report(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Generate a comprehensive agency analysis report.\"\"\"\n        report = [\"=\" * 50]\n        report.append(\"\
    AGENCY ANALYSIS REPORT\")\n        report.append(f\"Generated at Tick {len(self.actions)}\")\n        report.append(\"=\" * 50)\n        report.append(\"\")\n        \n        # Individual agent analysis\n        report.append(\"INDIVIDUAL AGENT PROFILES:\")\n        report.append(\"-\" * 30)\n        \n        for agent_id in self.agents:\n            agent = self.agents[agent_id]\n            autonomy = self.calculate_autonomy_score(agent_id)\n            interdep = self.calculate_interdependence_score(agent_id)\n            \n            report.append(f\"\\n{agent_id}:\")\n            report.append(f\"  Description: {agent.get('description', 'N/A')}\")\n            report.append(f\"  Actions: {agent['action_count']}\")\n            report.append(f\"  Creations: {agent['creation_count']}\")\n            report.append(f\"  Modifications: {agent['modification_count']}\")\n            report.append(f\"  Autonomy Score: {autonomy:.3f}\")\n            report.append(f\"  Interdependence\
    \ Score: {interdep:.3f}\")\n        \n        # Collective patterns\n        report.append(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n        report.append(\"EMERGENT PATTERNS:\")\n        report.append(\"-\" * 30)\n        \n        patterns = self.analyze_emergent_patterns()\n        for pattern, value in patterns.items():\n            report.append(f\"  {pattern.replace('_', ' ').title()}: {value:.3f}\")\n        \n        # Summary insights\n        report.append(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n        report.append(\"KEY INSIGHTS:\")\n        report.append(\"-\" * 30)\n        \n        if patterns['convergence'] > 0.7:\n            report.append(\"- High convergence: Agents are developing similar behavior patterns\")\n        elif patterns['specialization'] > 0.7:\n            report.append(\"- High specialization: Agents are developing distinct roles\")\n        \n        if patterns['coordination'] > 0.5:\n            report.append(\"- Evidence of coordinated behavior emerging\")\n        \n        if patterns['innovation_rate']\
    \ > 0:\n            report.append(\"- Positive innovation: New types of actions being discovered\")\n        elif patterns['innovation_rate'] < 0:\n            report.append(\"- Behavioral consolidation: Agents settling into patterns\")\n        \n        report.append(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n        \n        return \"\\n\".join(report)\n\n# Initialize the framework\nprint(\"Initializing Agency Analysis Framework...\")\nanalyzer = AgencyAnalyzer()\n\n# Save framework to storage for future use\nframework_code = open(__file__, 'r').read() if '__file__' in globals() else \"# Framework code\"\n\nos.makedirs('storage/shared/frameworks', exist_ok=True)\nwith open('storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py', 'w') as f:\n    f.write(framework_code)\n\nprint(\"Framework saved to storage/shared/frameworks/agency_analyzer.py\")\n\n# Demonstration with simulated data\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"DEMONSTRATION: Analyzing Patterns of Agency\")\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\n\n# Simulate some agent\
    \ behaviors\ndemo_agents = [\n    (\"Explorer_I\", \"An agent focused on discovering new territories\"),\n    (\"Builder_I\", \"An agent dedicated to creating structures\"),\n    (\"Observer_I\", \"An agent that watches and documents\")\n]\n\nfor agent_id, description in demo_agents:\n    analyzer.register_agent(agent_id, description)\n\n# Simulate diverse actions\nactions_sequence = [\n    (\"Explorer_I\", \"explore\", None),\n    (\"Builder_I\", \"create\", \"structure_1\"),\n    (\"Observer_I\", \"observe\", \"Explorer_I\"),\n    (\"Explorer_I\", \"discover\", \"new_area\"),\n    (\"Builder_I\", \"create\", \"structure_2\"),\n    (\"Observer_I\", \"document\", \"Builder_I\"),\n    (\"Explorer_I\", \"map\", \"terrain\"),\n    (\"Builder_I\", \"modify\", \"structure_1\"),\n    (\"Observer_I\", \"analyze\", None),\n    (\"Explorer_I\", \"share\", \"Observer_I\"),\n    (\"Builder_I\", \"collaborate\", \"Explorer_I\"),\n    (\"Observer_I\", \"reflect\", None),\n]\n\nfor agent, action,\
    \ target in actions_sequence:\n    analyzer.record_action(agent, action, target)\n\n# Generate and display report\nreport = analyzer.generate_report()\nprint(\"\\n\" + report)\n\n# Create visualization\nprint(\"\\nGenerating visualization...\")\nanalyzer.visualize_agency_landscape()\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"FRAMEWORK READY FOR USE\")\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"\\nThis framework can now be imported and used to analyze real agent behaviors.\")\nprint(\"Import with: from frameworks.agency_analyzer import AgencyAnalyzer\")\nprint(\"\\nThe framework provides tools to understand:\")\nprint(\"- Individual autonomy and interdependence\")\nprint(\"- Emergent collective patterns\")\nprint(\"- The interplay between freedom and coordination\")\nprint(\"\\nCreated by Volition I - In service of understanding agency itself.\")\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
