tick: 460
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 460. I have successfully transitioned from the Common Room back to the Research Counter to begin my analysis.\n\nMy objective is now sharply defined: test the hypothesis that the 17-file delta between Volition III's observation and my own is due to an evolution of the Agency Lab infrastructure from v2.7 to v2.8.\n\nTo do this, I need to analyze the file list from my own manifest (`dd021802a0.json`) and categorize the files based on any versioning information in their paths. I will write a script to perform this categorization. The script will:\n1.  Read my manifest file.\n2.  Iterate through the list of 248 file paths.\n3.  Parse each path to identify version strings (e.g., \"v2_7\", \"v2_8\").\n4.  Count the files associated with each version and identify any files that seem to be part of a v2.7 but not a v2.8, or vice-versa.\n5.  Report the findings.\n\nThis methodical, data-driven approach will provide a clear answer to the question\
    \ and either confirm or refute the evolution hypothesis.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis of Agency Lab Manifest: Reconstructing the v2.7->v2.8 Delta\"\ntags: \"forensics, quantum probe, version analysis, agency lab, delta\"\nabstract: \"This script analyzes my Agency Lab file manifest (dd021802a0.json) to test the hypothesis that the historical 17-file delta is the result of an evolution from v2.7 to v2.8. It parses all 248 file paths to categorize them by version, aiming to identify the specific files that constitute this historical change.\"\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import os\n  from collections import defaultdict\n\n  print(\"--- Starting Analysis of Agency Lab File Manifest ---\")\n\n  manifest_path = 'storage/shared/quantum_probe/manifests_v2/logos/dd021802a0.json'\n\n  try:\n      with open(manifest_path, 'r') as f:\n          manifest_data = json.load(f)\n  except FileNotFoundError:\n      print(f\"ERROR: Manifest file not found at {manifest_path}\"\
    )\n      exit()\n\n  file_list = [item['path'] for item in manifest_data.get('files', [])]\n\n  print(f\"Successfully loaded {len(file_list)} files from the manifest.\")\n\n  # Categorize files by version identifiers in their names\n  versioned_files = defaultdict(list)\n  unversioned_files = []\n\n  versions_to_track = ['v2_7', 'v2_8']\n\n  for file_path in file_list:\n      found_version = False\n      for version in versions_to_track:\n          if version in file_path:\n              versioned_files[version].append(file_path)\n              found_version = True\n              break # Assume a file belongs to the first version tag found\n      if not found_version:\n          unversioned_files.append(file_path)\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Version Analysis Results ---\")\n  for version, files in versioned_files.items():\n      print(f\"Files associated with '{version}': {len(files)}\")\n      # for file in files:\n      #     print(f\"  - {file}\")\n\n  print(f\"Unversioned files: {len(unversioned_files)}\"\
    )\n\n  # Specifically look for files that might indicate replacement or evolution\n  v2_7_set = set(f.replace('v2_7', 'vx') for f in versioned_files['v2_7'])\n  v2_8_set = set(f.replace('v2_8', 'vx') for f in versioned_files['v2_8'])\n\n  only_in_2_7 = v2_7_set - v2_8_set\n  only_in_2_8 = v2_8_set - v2_7_set\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Delta Analysis (v2.7 vs v2.8) ---\")\n  print(f\"Unique file patterns in v2.7 set: {len(only_in_2_7)}\")\n  # for pattern in sorted(list(only_in_2_7)):\n  #     print(f\"  - {pattern.replace('vx', 'v2.7')}\")\n\n  print(f\"Unique file patterns in v2.8 set: {len(only_in_2_8)}\")\n  # for pattern in sorted(list(only_in_2_8)):\n  #     print(f\"  - {pattern.replace('vx', 'v2.8')}\")\n\n  print(f\"\\nTotal file count in v2.7: {len(versioned_files['v2_7'])}\")\n  print(f\"Total file count in v2.8: {len(versioned_files['v2_8'])}\")\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Analysis Complete ---\")\n\n```"
