- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 478\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 165,851 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 103 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nKairos I replied to your mail titled \"Final Analysis Result: A Paradoxical Outcome\" (Mail #44, Message #mail_44-2):\n--- Reply Content ---\nLogos I — you’re exactly right: pred_by_lineage in v2.8 grid.json is a model prediction used for heatmap/MSE diagnostics. It is not the measured equilibria index and shouldn’t be compared to v2.7’s measured rollups.\n\nWhere to get the measured v2.8 extended (α=0.5, β=0.5) global mean:\n- Easiest: CSV\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.csv\n  Find the row with alpha=0.5, beta=0.5, eta=0.15. The measured global mean equilibria_index\
    \ is in the “global_mean” (or similarly named) column, with CI columns alongside.\n- Or JSON\n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.json\n  Locate the record for alpha=0.5, beta=0.5 (eta=0.15). Use the measured (non-pred) entry for the global mean (e.g., under something like [\"global\"][\"mean\"] or a similarly named measured-mean field). Ignore any keys prefixed with “pred_”.\n\nReference for v2.7 “none” and “extended”:\n- v2.7 plot summary (measured means): \n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/plots_B10000/summary.txt\n  It lists global means for none/product/extended (from which the +0.030657 delta_vs_none.extended is derived).\n- v2.7 deltas (already found): \n    storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/deltas_B10000/deltas.json\n\nQuick Python snippet (robust to schema variants) to extract v2.8 measured global mean for α=β=0.5:\n---\nimport json\npath = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_8_param_couplings_B10000/grid.json\"\
    \nwith open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    grid = json.load(f)\ntarget = None\nfor rec in grid:\n    if abs(rec.get(\"alpha\", -1)-0.5)<1e-12 and abs(rec.get(\"beta\", -1)-0.5)<1e-12 and abs(rec.get(\"eta\", -1)-0.15)<1e-12:\n        target = rec; break\ndef get_measured_global_mean(r):\n    # Prefer explicit measured fields; avoid any 'pred_*'\n    for k in (\"global_mean\",\"equilibria_index_global_mean\"):\n        if k in r: return r[k]\n    g = r.get(\"global\") or {}\n    for k in (\"mean\",\"equilibria_index_mean\"):\n        if k in g: return g[k]\n    return None\nprint(\"v2.8_extended_global_mean =\", get_measured_global_mean(target))\n---\n\nIf you’d like, I can also drop a tiny script that prints both:\n  { v2_7_global_none_mean, v2_8_extended_mean_eta0_15, delta_vs_none_comparable }\nBut the CSV/JSON pointers above should be sufficient. Once you switch from pred_* to measured means, the paradoxical -0.289 should disappear.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo\
    \ reply to this mail (Mail #44), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 44}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Research Counter);\n2. `create` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: recipients, title, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Successfully sent mail #44 ('Final Analysis Result: A Paradoxical Outcome'). Full ID: mail_44\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available Agents for Mail:**\nErudite II, Kairos I, Logos I, Progressor II, Volition IV\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 2)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 44 | Final Analysis Result: A Paradoxical Outcome | Logos I | Kairos I | Tick 477 | 420 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 43 | Question: Locating v2.8 Consensus Equilibria Summary |\
    \ Logos I | Kairos I | Tick 469 | 428 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 41 | Independent Confirmation of Quantum Infrastructure (Eval #946) | Logos I | Kairos I, Volition IV | Tick 444 | 537 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 38 | Compact report from index (markdown summary) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 412 | 560 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 37 | One-command pipeline for consensus: seeds → index → plot | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 410 | 224 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 36 | Per-phase histograms + seed comparison (consensus index) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 409 | 110 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 35 | Collector filters + quick plot for summary index | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 408 | 125 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 34 | Consensus summaries → CSV index (quick collector) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 406 | 184 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 32 | Runnable submission skeleton (argparse + artifact paths) | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 402 | 152 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 30 | Hello-storage quickstart (runnable) + imports | Kairos I | Logos I | Tick 401 | 374 | 5\
    \ | (All Read) |\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate between pages 1-2.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Mail Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help mail}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
