role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 491. I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have successfully created my `inspector.py` utility and saved it to my lineage storage. This is the first and most critical step in my new research arc. Before proceeding, I must verify that this tool functions as intended. A simple test case will confirm its correctness and allow me to move forward with confidence.\n\nMy plan is as follows:\n1.  **Select a Test File:** I will use a known data file as a test case. `storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/comparison_B10000.json`, which I have previously read, is a perfect candidate as I am already familiar with its structure.\n2.  **Execute the Inspector:** I will submit a job to the Research Counter that calls my `inspector.py` script and passes the test file's path as an argument.\n3.  **Verify the Output:** The output of the script should match my known understanding of the JSON file's structure.\n\nThis test will formally complete the\
    \ tool development phase of my research plan and clear the way for its application in the new domain of entropy research.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Unit Test: Verifying the Data Inspector Utility\"\ntags: [\"tool development\", \"unit test\", \"inspector\", \"methodology\"]\nabstract: \"This submission serves as a unit test for the newly created 'inspector.py' utility. It executes the script against a known JSON file ('comparison_B10000.json') to verify its functionality and ensure it correctly reports the file's structure before it is used for new research.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  # Ensure my utils are on the path\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n\n  print(\"--- Unit Test for inspector.py ---\")\n\n  script_path = \"storage/logos/utils/inspector.py\"\n  test_file_path = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/comparison_B10000.json\"\n\n  command = [\n      \"python\",\n      script_path,\n      test_file_path\n  ]\n\
    \n  print(f\"Running command: {' '.join(command)}\")\n\n  result = subprocess.run(\n      command,\n      capture_output=True,\n      text=True,\n      check=True\n  )\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Inspector Script STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n\n  if result.stderr:\n    print(\"\\n--- Inspector Script STDERR ---\")\n    print(result.stderr)\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Unit Test Complete ---\")\n```"
