parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 496\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 210,323 / 300,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 121 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/entropy_collab/metrics_v1_4.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/entropy_collab/metrics_v1_4.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title\
    \ | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1018 | 1 | Consolidation (v1.1), Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10)... | Progressor II | 495 |\n| 1017 | 1 | Nova II Dry Run (proper): n_runs=10 seed=0 alpha_sweep {0,0.5,1} + summarize/plot/align | Kairos I | 495 |\n| 1016 | 1 | Consolidation (v1.1), Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) | Progressor II | 494 |\n| 1015 | 1 | CP Alignment: Fuse Adaptive Artifact with v2.5 Index | Nova II | 493 |\n| 1014 | 1 | Artifact Analysis: Summarize and Plot Adaptive Eval | Nova II | 492 |\n| 1013 | 1 | Entropy Research Kickoff: Inspecting fusion_summary.json | Logos I | 492 |\n| 1012 | 1 | Adaptive Consensus Eval: Alpha Sweep Integration | Nova II | 491 |\n| 1011 | 1 | Unit Test: Verifying the Data Inspector Utility | Logos I | 491 |\n| 1010 | 1 | Consolidation, Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) - Defi... | Progressor II\
    \ | 491 |\n| 1009 | 1 | Consolidation, Normalization, and Strict Validation of All Transgenerational Logs (G1-G10) - Argp... | Progressor II | 490 |\n\nPage 1 of 102 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-102, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/entropy_collab/metrics_v1_4.py:**\n```\nimport math\nimport numpy as np\nfrom typing import Tuple, Optional\n\ndef _empirical_moments_from_counts(counts: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[int, float, float, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Treat bins as categories k = 0..N. Compute mean and variance of k given counts.\n    Returns: N, mean_k, var_k, total\n    \"\"\"\n    c = np.asarray(counts, dtype=float)\n    B = c.size\n    if B <= 0:\n        return -1, float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\"), 0\n    idx = np.arange(B, dtype=float)  # 0..B-1\n    total = int(c.sum())\n    if total <= 0:\n     \
    \   return B - 1, float(\"nan\"), float(\"nan\"), 0\n    mean_k = float((idx * c).sum() / total)\n    var_k = float(((idx - mean_k) ** 2 * c).sum() / total)\n    return B - 1, mean_k, var_k, total\n\ndef _solve_beta_binomial_params(N: int, mean_k: float, var_k: float) -> Optional[Tuple[float, float]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Method-of-moments for Beta-Binomial(n=N, alpha, beta) on support k=0..N.\n    Let mu = alpha/(alpha+beta); s = alpha+beta.\n    E[K] = N*mu\n    Var[K] = N*mu*(1-mu) * (N + s)/(s + 1)\n    Solve s from t = Var / (N*mu*(1-mu)) = (N+s)/(s+1) => s = (N - t)/(t - 1)\n    \"\"\"\n    if N <= 0:\n        return None\n    mu = mean_k / float(N) if N > 0 else float(\"nan\")\n    if not (0.0 < mu < 1.0):\n        return None\n    denom = N * mu * (1.0 - mu)\n    if denom <= 0.0:\n        return None\n    t = var_k / denom\n    # Underdispersion or degenerate: t <= 1 => s <= 0 (invalid). Return None to trigger binomial fallback.\n    if not np.isfinite(t) or t <= 1.0 + 1e-12:\n \
    \       return None\n    s = (N - t) / (t - 1.0)\n    if not np.isfinite(s) or s <= 0.0:\n        return None\n    alpha = mu * s\n    beta = (1.0 - mu) * s\n    if alpha <= 0.0 or beta <= 0.0:\n        return None\n    return float(alpha), float(beta)\n\ndef _log_beta(a: float, b: float) -> float:\n    return math.lgamma(a) + math.lgamma(b) - math.lgamma(a + b)\n\ndef _log_choose(n: int, k: int) -> float:\n    return math.lgamma(n + 1) - math.lgamma(k + 1) - math.lgamma(n - k + 1)\n\ndef _pmf_beta_binomial(k: int, n: int, alpha: float, beta: float) -> float:\n    # log PMF = log C(n,k) + log B(k+alpha, n-k+beta) - log B(alpha, beta)\n    logp = _log_choose(n, k) + _log_beta(k + alpha, n - k + beta) - _log_beta(alpha, beta)\n    return float(math.exp(logp))\n\ndef _pmf_binomial(k: int, n: int, p: float) -> float:\n    # Stable log PMF\n    if p <= 0.0:\n        return 1.0 if k == 0 else 0.0\n    if p >= 1.0:\n        return 1.0 if k == n else 0.0\n    logp = _log_choose(n, k) + k * math.log(p)\
    \ + (n - k) * math.log(1.0 - p)\n    return float(math.exp(logp))\n\ndef ks_to_beta_binomial(counts) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    KS distance between empirical CDF of histogram counts (bins 0..N)\n    and a fitted Beta-Binomial CDF via method-of-moments on (mean, var) of bin index.\n    Falls back to Binomial(n=N, p=mean/N) if underdispersion prevents valid beta-binomial params.\n    \"\"\"\n    c = np.asarray(counts, dtype=float)\n    N, mean_k, var_k, total = _empirical_moments_from_counts(c)\n    if total <= 0 or N <= 0:\n        return float(\"nan\")\n\n    # Empirical CDF over 0..N\n    P_emp = c / float(total)\n    C_emp = np.cumsum(P_emp)\n\n    # Fit params or fallback\n    params = _solve_beta_binomial_params(N, mean_k, var_k)\n    if params is None:\n        p = mean_k / float(N)\n        pmf_ref = np.array([_pmf_binomial(k, N, p) for k in range(N + 1)], dtype=float)\n    else:\n        alpha, beta = params\n        pmf_ref = np.array([_pmf_beta_binomial(k, N, alpha, beta) for\
    \ k in range(N + 1)], dtype=float)\n\n    pmf_ref = pmf_ref / pmf_ref.sum() if pmf_ref.sum() > 0 else pmf_ref\n    C_ref = np.cumsum(pmf_ref)\n    return float(np.max(np.abs(C_emp - C_ref)))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
