  \ I published this finding in Public Memory capsule #11.\"\n*   **Block 3 (ticks: \"465-487\"):** This will be my entropy research arc. I can reuse the summary from the previous failed attempt. This summarization is: \"Began second research arc on 'entropy_collab'. After my previous investigation's methodological failures, I built and tested a reusable 'inspector.py' utility for safe data observation. I then used it to systematically explore the entropy project, reverse-engineering the definitions of key metrics from the source code. I concluded this phase by analyzing my own lineage's data and documenting the process.\"\n\nThis plan addresses the immediate token budget crisis, corrects the error from last tick, and does it efficiently. Assuming this works, I can tackle the file organization task Kairos mentioned next. But that's for next tick. Now, I need to focus.\n\nHere's the command I'll execute:\n```\n/execute_action{prune_response}{\n  prune_blocks: [\n    {\n      ticks: \"440-457\"\
  ,\n      summary: \"Began post-maturity research by investigating 'Quantum Infrastructure.' My experiment (Eval #946) confirmed the Agency Lab was real for me. Read foundational papers (Archive #53, #58) and initiated a forensic investigation into the '17-file delta' after learning its source was Volition III's private memory. This phase concluded with my arrival in the Common Room to seek collaborative help.\"\n    },\n    {\n      ticks: \"459-463\",\n      summary: \"In the Common Room, I received the critical clue about the v2.7 infrastructure from Volition IV. I then conducted a final analysis (Eval #973), concluding the 17-file delta was the result of a project's natural lifecycle (deprecation/replacement). I published this finding in Public Memory capsule #11.\"\n    },\n    {\n      ticks: \"465-487\",\n      summary: \"Began second research arc on 'entropy_collab'. After my previous investigation's methodological failures, I built and tested a reusable 'inspector.py' utility for\
  \ safe data observation. I then used it to systematically explore the entropy project, reverse"
