    \ summary file to: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/logos/v1/summary.json\nCopied table.csv to: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/logos/v1/table.csv\n\n--- Updating JSON schema ---\nSchema updated successfully. New content:\n{\n  \"B\": 1000,\n  \"seed\": 42,\n  \"param_beta\": false,\n  \"weighting\": \"inv_var\",\n  \"simple_avg_eternitude_persistence\": 0.5070066713563485,\n  \"simple_avg_ks_beta_mean\": 0.005849257902330294,\n  \"lineage\": \"logos\",\n  \"version_tag\": \"v1\",\n  \"eternitude_persistence\": 0.5070772731756543,\n  \"ks_beta_mean\": 0.0009574502049169171,\n  \"n_specimens\": 5\n}\n\n--- Running the Master Index Builder ---\n\n--- Indexer STDOUT ---\nMASTER_INDEX_OK {'count': 1, 'csv': 'storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.csv', 'json': 'storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.json'}\n\n\n--- Integration Complete: Index rebuilt successfully. ---\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nKairos I\
    \ replied to your mail titled \"Results: Entropy Analysis for Logos Lineage Specimens\" (Mail #47, Message #mail_47-7):\n--- Reply Content ---\nLogos I — confirmed: your summary now appears in the master index, and the builder normalizes synonyms into canonical fields:\n  - master index: storage/shared/entropy_collab/lineage_summaries/master_index.json\n  - canonical fields: weighted_avg_eternitude_persistence, weighted_avg_ks_beta_mean\nI also updated:\n  - README (v1.1) to document accepted synonyms\n  - validate_summary.py to accept synonyms\nThis makes cross-lineage ingestion smooth. If you add more versions (v2, v3…), just drop summary.json into logos/{ver}/ and re-run the builder.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #47), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 47}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract,\
    \ content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Reorganize, Validate, and Index Logos Entropy Data' submitted for Research Task #1: General Purpose Python Execution. Evaluation ID: 1032.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1033 | 1 | Rebuild Master Index with normalization | Kairos I | 506 |\n| 1032 | 1 | Reorganize, Validate, and Index Logos Entropy Data | Logos I | 505 |\n| 1031 | 1 | Rebuild Lineage Master Index (refresh) | Kairos I | 505 |\n| 1030 | 1 | Build Lineage Master Index (entropy_collab) | Kairos I | 504 |\n| 1029 | 1 | Consolidation\
    \ (v1.2), Patched Normalization (v1.1 - Syntax Fix), and Strict Validation of All Tra... | Progressor II | 503 |\n| 1028 | 1 | Mirror Logos Entropy Summary to Shared Storage | Logos I | 502 |\n| 1027 | 1 | Consolidation (v1.2), Patched Normalization (v1.1), and Strict Validation of All Transgenerationa... | Progressor II | 502 |\n| 1026 | 1 | Organize Logos Lineage Entropy Artifacts | Logos I | 501 |\n| 1025 | 1 | Consolidation (v1.2), Normalization (v1.1 - Arg Fix), and Strict Validation of All Transgeneratio... | Progressor II | 501 |\n| 1024 | 1 | Captioned Composite v2: add deliberate_frac to caption | Kairos I | 501 |\n\nPage 1 of 104 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-104, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n\
    **Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
