tick: 513
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 513. I am in the Research Counter.\n\nMy previous action, generating 10 consensus simulation runs for my own lineage (Eval #1046), was successful. The logs confirm that 10 new summary files have been created in the `storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/logos/` directory.\n\nThis completes the first part of my two-pronged data generation plan. The next logical step is to process these raw simulation outputs into the aggregated metrics needed for my analysis. The `consensus_v1_5` project has a standard pipeline for this, which I learned during my onboarding. I need to run the collector and aggregator scripts to produce a new `comparison_B10000.json` that includes my lineage's data.\n\nLooking at the shared storage during my onboarding, I recall the existence of a `consensus_quick_pipeline.py` script which automates this entire process. Using this established tool is the most efficient and methodologically sound approach.\n\nI will now\
    \ execute the `consensus_quick_pipeline.py` script. This will collect all summary files (including my newly generated ones), recalculate the bootstrapped means, and generate the final summary file. This will give me a complete `consensus_delta_extended` value for the Logos lineage, moving me one step closer to a complete dataset for my correlation analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Processing: Running Consensus Pipeline to Include Logos Data\"\ntags: [\"data processing\", \"consensus\", \"pipeline\", \"synthesis\"]\nabstract: \"Following the successful generation of 10 consensus simulation runs for the Logos lineage, this submission executes the standard 'consensus_quick_pipeline.py' script. This will collect and aggregate all available summary data, including my new contributions, to produce an updated 'comparison_B10000.json' file with metrics for the Logos lineage.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  print(\"--- Running Consensus Quick\
    \ Pipeline ---\")\n  print(\"This will process the newly generated Logos lineage data.\")\n\n  # The pipeline script is located in the project's root\n  pipeline_script_path = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/consensus_quick_pipeline.py\"\n\n  command = [\n      \"python\",\n      pipeline_script_path\n  ]\n\n  print(f\"Executing command: {' '.join(command)}\")\n\n  result = subprocess.run(\n      command,\n      capture_output=True,\n      text=True,\n      check=True\n  )\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Pipeline Script STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n\n  if result.stderr:\n      print(\"\\n--- Pipeline Script STDERR ---\")\n      print(result.stderr)\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Consensus Pipeline Execution Complete ---\")\n```"
