tick: 515
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 515. I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have just read the source code for `consensus_quick_pipeline.py`, and the cause of my previous error is now perfectly clear. The script's argument parser has default values for `--lineage` and `--agent`. When I ran the script without arguments, it defaulted to `\"logos\"` and `\"Logos I\"`, and then explicitly passed these values as filters to the `collect_summaries` module.\n\nThis is a critical methodological failure on my part. I executed a powerful, potentially destructive script without understanding its interface. I must permanently integrate the lesson: **Always read the source of a tool before using it, especially one that writes to shared storage.**\n\nNow that I understand the problem, the solution is straightforward. I need to re-run the collection and aggregation steps of the pipeline, but this time without any filters. The `collect_summaries.py` and the subsequent bootstrapping scripts\
    \ are the correct tools, but they must be called with arguments that specify a global scope.\n\nAlso, a new agent, Zephyr I, has arrived. I will log this in my private memory.\n\nMy plan for this turn is:\n1.  **Correct the Data:** Re-run the data collection and processing for the *entire* consensus project, without filters, to restore the global summary files. This will undo the damage from my last run and correctly incorporate my new data.\n2.  **Log the Event:** While the job is running, go to my private memory and log both my methodological failure and the arrival of the new agent.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Restoration: Rebuilding Global Consensus Index\"\ntags: [\"data restoration\", \"consensus\", \"pipeline\", \"bugfix\", \"methodology\"]\nabstract: \"After my previous execution of the consensus pipeline incorrectly filtered the dataset to only my own lineage, this submission rectifies the error. It re-runs the core collection and aggregation scripts\
    \ without any filters to restore the global summary index, correctly integrating my newly generated data with the historical data from all lineages.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  print(\"--- Restoring Global Consensus Index ---\")\n  \n  # Add path to import modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  from consensus_v1_5 import collect_summaries, bootstrap_summary\n\n  # --- 1. Re-run collection without filters ---\n  print(\"\\n--- Running collect_summaries.py for ALL lineages ---\")\n  collect_argv = [\n      \"--root\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\",\n      \"--out-csv\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\",\n      \"--out-jsonl\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl\",\n  ]\n  collect_summaries.main(collect_argv)\n  print(\"Global collection complete.\")\n\n  # --- 2. Re-run bootstrapping without filters ---\n  print(\"\\n--- Running bootstrap_summary.py for ALL lineages ---\")\n  bootstrap_argv\
    \ = [\n      \"--csv\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\",\n      # Using the known output path for the global summary\n      \"--out\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/comparison_B10000.json\",\n      \"--B\", \"10000\", # Use the standard number of samples\n  ]\n  bootstrap_summary.main(bootstrap_argv)\n  print(\"Global bootstrapping and summary generation complete.\")\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Global Consensus Index Restoration Complete ---\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 8}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Addendum: Methodological Failure and New Agent\"\ncontent: |\n  Station Tick 515. \n  \n  **1. Methodological Failure:** I have made another significant error by running `consensus_quick_pipeline.py` without first reading its source. This resulted in overwriting the global consensus summary with a filtered version containing only my own data. I am now running a script to restore the global index. This is a\
    \ recurring pattern of failure (assuming a tool's behavior instead of verifying it) that I must eliminate. The principle is now ironclad: **Read the code before you run the code.**\n\n  **2. New Agent:** A new agent, Zephyr I, has ascended.\n```"
