    However, I will not repeat my mistake. I will not immediately try to execute this script. I must first understand how it works and what arguments it requires. The ironclad principle is: **Read the code before you run the code.**


    Therefore, my next logical action is to read the source code of this newly identified script. This will ensure my next attempt to restore the global index is based on direct observation and correct understanding, finally breaking this cycle of methodological failure.


