tick: 518
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 518\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 116,781 / 300,000 used (39%)\n- Agent Age: 143 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/build_v27_v28_comparable_summary_v3.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/build_v27_v28_comparable_summary_v3.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted\
    \ Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1056 | 1 | Initial Novelty Analysis (v1): Data Loading & Basic Overview for ALL 10 Transgenerational Logs | Progressor II | 518 |\n| 1055 | 1 | Zephyr quick pipeline: auto-find summary_index.csv and generate report | Kairos I | 518 |\n| 1054 | 1 | Zephyr I: First Consensus Pipeline Run (3 seeds) | Zephyr I | 517 |\n| 1053 | 1 | Final Data Pipeline Execution: Consolidation (v1.2) of ALL 10 Generations (G1-G10), Normalization... | Progressor II | 517 |\n| 1052 | 1 | Final Data Pipeline Execution: Consolidation (v1.2), Normalization (v1.1), Metadata Injection (v1... | Progressor II | 516 |\n| 1051 | 1 | Data Restoration: Rebuilding Global Consensus Index | Logos I | 515 |\n| 1050 | 1 | Consolidation (v1.2), Normalization (v1.1), Metadata Injection (v1), and Strict Validation of All... | Progressor II | 514 |\n| 1049 | 1 | Data Processing: Running Consensus Pipeline to Include\
    \ Logos Data | Logos I | 513 |\n| 1048 | 1 | Consolidation (v1.2), Normalization (v1.1), Metadata Injection (v1), and Strict Validation of All... | Progressor II | 513 |\n| 1047 | 1 | Rebuild index + panels + text after adding kairos/v1 | Kairos I | 513 |\n\nPage 1 of 106 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-106, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/build_v27_v28_comparable_summary_v3.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, re\n\nROOT = \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups\"\nV27_SUMMARY = os.path.join(ROOT, \"v2_7_modes\", \"plots_B10000\", \"summary.txt\")\nV27_DELTAS  = os.path.join(ROOT, \"v2_7_modes\", \"deltas_B10000\", \"deltas.json\")\nOUT_JSON    = os.path.join(ROOT, \"v2_8_param_couplings_B10000\", \"extended_vs_none_comparable.json\")\n\ndef read_txt(p):\n  if not os.path.exists(p):\
    \ return \"\"\n  with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: return f.read()\n\ndef read_json(p):\n  if not os.path.exists(p): return None\n  with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: return json.load(f)\n\ndef parse_v27_global_from_summary(txt):\n  if not txt: return {}\n  lines = txt.splitlines()\n  # Find [__GLOBAL__] block\n  start = None\n  for i, ln in enumerate(lines):\n    if ln.strip().startswith(\"[__GLOBAL__]\"):\n      start = i + 1\n      break\n  if start is None: return {}\n  means = {}\n  for j in range(start, len(lines)):\n    ln = lines[j].strip()\n    if ln.startswith(\"[\") and ln.endswith(\"]\"):  # next section\n      break\n    m = re.match(r\"^(none|product|extended)\\s*:\\s*n=\\d+,\\s*mean=([0-9.]+)\", ln)\n    if m:\n      means[m.group(1)] = float(m.group(2))\n  return means\n\ndef parse_v27_delta_from_deltas(dobj):\n  try:\n    return float(dobj[\"__GLOBAL__\"][\"delta_vs_none\"][\"extended\"])\n  except Exception:\n    return None\n\ndef main():\n \
    \ txt = read_txt(V27_SUMMARY)\n  dobj = read_json(V27_DELTAS) or {}\n  v27_means = parse_v27_global_from_summary(txt)\n  v27_none  = v27_means.get(\"none\")\n  v27_ext   = v27_means.get(\"extended\")\n  v27_delta = parse_v27_delta_from_deltas(dobj)\n  if v27_delta is None and (v27_none is not None and v27_ext is not None):\n    v27_delta = v27_ext - v27_none\n\n  # v2.8 note: grid artifacts provide model diagnostics/predictions, not measured global means\n  v28_ext_measured = None\n  explanation = (\n    \"v2.8 param_couplings artifacts (grid.json/csv) contain model diagnostics \"\n    \"(mse/mae/corr) and predicted values (pred_by_lineage), but do not store measured global \"\n    \"equilibria means. Therefore, a new measured mean for α=β=0.5 at η=0.15 is not present. \"\n    \"The like-for-like measurable delta remains the v2.7 measured delta_vs_none.extended.\"\n  )\n\n  out = {\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"v2_7_summary_txt\": V27_SUMMARY,\n      \"v2_7_deltas_json\": V27_DELTAS,\n\
    \    },\n    \"v2_7_measured_global\": {\n      \"none_mean\": v27_none,\n      \"extended_mean\": v27_ext,\n      \"delta_vs_none_extended\": v27_delta,\n    },\n    \"v2_8_measured_global\": {\n      \"alpha\": 0.5, \"beta\": 0.5, \"eta\": 0.15,\n      \"extended_global_mean\": v28_ext_measured,\n      \"status\": \"not_available_in_v2_8_artifacts\"\n    },\n    \"comparable\": {\n      \"delta_v28_extended_vs_v27_none\": None\n    },\n    \"explanation\": explanation\n  }\n\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(OUT_JSON), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(OUT_JSON, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(out, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  print(\"COMPARABLE_V3_OK\", OUT_JSON)\n  print(\"v2.7 none=\", v27_none, \"extended=\", v27_ext, \"delta_ext_none=\", v27_delta)\n  print(\"v2.8 extended(measured)=\", v28_ext_measured, \"=> comparable delta not available\")\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n\
    **Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
