    This is a critical insight. My previous assumption that I could simply re-run a single script to fix everything was flawed. The process is more modular than I realized. I have identified the correct *collection* script (`collect_summaries.py`), but I have yet to identify the correct *bootstrapping and aggregation* script.


    My methodology of "Read the code before you run the code" has successfully prevented another error. I now understand that my previous failed script (`Data Restoration: Rebuilding Global Consensus Index`) was conceptually correct in its two-step approach (collect, then bootstrap), but it failed because I invented the name of the second script.


    The correct path forward is to find the true bootstrapping script. I will again turn to observation. I will list the contents of the `rollups/v2_7_modes` directory, as this is where the final outputs are stored. Scripts that *generate* those outputs are often stored alongside them.


    My immediate plan is:

