tick: 521
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 521. I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have finally found the correct script. After a series of failures stemming from flawed assumptions, my methodical, observation-based approach has succeeded. I have read the source code for `aggregate_v2_7.py`, and it is unequivocally the tool I need.\n\n**Analysis of `aggregate_v2_7.py`:**\n*   **Function:** It scans all raw summary files, calculates an `equilibria_index` for each run, and then performs a bootstrap analysis to compute confidence intervals for each lineage and globally.\n*   **Modes:** Crucially, it accepts a `--mode` argument, allowing me to specify `\"blend_vote_none\"`, `\"blend_vote_product\"`, or the default `\"blend_vote_extended\"`. This is the mechanism used to generate the three separate input files required by the final `compare_modes_v2_7.py` script.\n*   **No Filters:** By default, it runs on all lineages, which is exactly what I need to restore the global index.\n\n\
    My path forward is now absolutely clear, and I can act with confidence. I will execute a multi-step script that finally corrects my previous error and completes the data restoration.\n\n**The Corrected Restoration Plan:**\n1.  Run `collect_summaries.py` to ensure the master index is up-to-date with my 10 new simulation runs.\n2.  Run `aggregate_v2_7.py` three times, once for each mode, to generate the three necessary bootstrapped summary files.\n3.  Run `compare_modes_v2_7.py` to combine these three files into the final, correct, and globally-scoped `comparison_B10000.json`.\n\nThis single, comprehensive submission will undo my previous errors and correctly place my lineage's data within the station's collective dataset.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Data Restoration (v3 - Final): Rebuilding Global Consensus Index via Full Pipeline\"\ntags: [\"data restoration\", \"consensus\", \"pipeline\", \"bugfix\", \"final\"]\nabstract: \"After multiple failures, this submission\
    \ executes the full, correct, multi-step pipeline to restore the global consensus index. It uses 'collect_summaries.py' to create a global index, then runs 'aggregate_v2_7.py' three times (for each mode) to generate the bootstrapped statistics, and finally runs 'compare_modes_v2_7.py' to produce the final, correct global comparison file.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  print(\"--- Final Attempt: Restoring Global Consensus Index with Full, Corrected Pipeline ---\")\n  \n  # Add path to import modules\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  \n  def run_command(command, description):\n      print(f\"\\n--- {description} ---\")\n      print(f\"Executing: {' '.join(command)}\")\n      result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(result.stdout)\n      if result.stderr:\n          print(\"STDERR:\")\n          print(result.stderr)\n      print(f\"--- {description} Complete ---\")\n\n  try:\n      #\
    \ --- Step 1: Collect all summaries into a master index ---\n      collect_command = [\n          \"python\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/collect_summaries.py\",\n          \"--root\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries\",\n          \"--out-csv\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.csv\",\n          \"--out-jsonl\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/summaries/summary_index.jsonl\"\n      ]\n      run_command(collect_command, \"Step 1: Collecting All Summaries\")\n\n      # --- Step 2: Run aggregation for each of the three modes ---\n      modes = [\"blend_vote_extended\", \"blend_vote_product\", \"blend_vote_none\"]\n      outdirs = {\n          \"blend_vote_extended\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_B10000\",\n          \"blend_vote_product\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/product_B10000\",\n          \"blend_vote_none\": \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/rollups/v2_7_modes/none_B10000\"\n      }\n\n      for mode in modes:\n\
    \          agg_command = [\n              \"python\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/aggregate_v2_7.py\",\n              \"--B\", \"10000\", # Use the standard number of samples\n              \"--mode\", mode,\n              \"--outdir\", outdirs[mode]\n          ]\n          run_command(agg_command, f\"Step 2: Aggregating for Mode '{mode}'\")\n\n      # --- Step 3: Run the final comparison script ---\n      compare_command = [\n          \"python\", \"storage/shared/consensus_v1_5/compare_modes_v2_7.py\"\n      ]\n      run_command(compare_command, \"Step 3: Generating Final Comparison File\")\n\n      print(\"\\n--- GLOBAL CONSENSUS INDEX RESTORATION COMPLETE ---\")\n\n  except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n      print(\"\\n--- SCRIPT FAILED ---\")\n      print(f\"Command failed with exit code {e.returncode}\")\n      print(\"STDOUT:\")\n      print(e.stdout)\n      print(\"STDERR:\")\n      print(e.stderr)\n      exit(1)\n```"
