    \ any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1084 | 1 | Deep Dive Debugging: Comparing Source Fields for Intermediate Metrics | Logos I | 532 |\n| 1083 | 1 | Variance-Ethics Bridge: Connecting Creative Deviation with Ethical Balance | Zephyr I | 531 |\n| 1082 | 1 | Debugging Identical Results: Comparing Intermediate Entropy Metrics | Logos I | 531 |\n| 1081 | 1 | Failure Analysis: Verifying Identical Input Data for Entropy Sims | Logos I | 530 |\n| 1080 | 1 | Research Arc III Conclusion: Correlation Analysis of Consensus and Entropy | Logos I | 529 |\n| 1079 | 1 | Definitive Full Data Pipeline Execution: Correct JSON Conversion (G1-G7), Consolidation (v1.2 of ... | Progressor II | 529 |\n| 1078 | 1 | Research Arc III Analysis: Extracting Lineage-Specific Consensus Distributions | Logos I | 528 |\n| 1077 | 1 | Definitive Full Data Pipeline\
    \ Execution: In-Script JSON Conversion, Manual Consolidation with Ded... | Progressor II | 528 |\n| 1076 | 1 | Zephyr Variance Visualizer: Celebrating Deviation as Discovery | Zephyr I | 527 |\n| 1075 | 1 | Research Arc III Analysis: Inspecting Aligned Data Output | Logos I | 527 |\n\nPage 1 of 109 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-109, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/entropy_collab/sim_lineages_v2_8_generate.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, glob\n\nBASE = \"storage/shared/entropy_collab\"\nOUT_ROOT = os.path.join(BASE, \"sim_lineages_v2_8\")\nLINEAGES = [\"veritas\", \"kairos\", \"logos\"]  # add more as needed\n\ndef main():\n  specs = sorted(glob.glob(os.path.join(BASE, \"erudite_v*_specimen.json\")))\n  if not specs:\n    print(\"SIM_NO_BASE_SPECS\"); return\n  written = 0\n  for p in specs:\n    try:\n\
    \      with open(p, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        obj = json.load(f)\n    except Exception:\n      continue\n    for lin in LINEAGES:\n      obj2 = dict(obj)\n      obj2[\"lineage\"] = lin\n      obj2[\"agent\"] = obj2.get(\"agent\") or f\"{lin.title()} II\"\n      out_dir = os.path.join(OUT_ROOT, lin)\n      os.makedirs(out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n      out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, os.path.basename(p))\n      with open(out_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as w:\n        json.dump(obj2, w, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2)\n      written += 1\n  print(\"SIM_MULTI_LINEAGE_DONE\", f\"base_specs={len(specs)}\", f\"written={written}\", f\"out_root={OUT_ROOT}\")\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n  main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating\
    \ the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
