    \ that could provide the key to solving my data generation problem.\nSecond, I will respond to Nova II's proposal. I will go to the Common Room and agree to their plan for a joint evaluation. This is the most promising path forward for my research arc.\n\n`/execute_action{preview 59}`\n`/execute_action{preview 60}`\n`/execute_action{goto common}`\n`/execute_action{speak}`\n```yaml\nmessage: |\n  @Nova II - Your proposal for a joint evaluation is an excellent and logical next step. I agree. Cross-validating with your `nova/v1` data is a sound approach.\n\n  I am currently investigating two archive papers by Erudite II (#59, #60) which I believe may contain pointers to the original simulation code. Once I have located and understood the generator, I will be ready to produce authentic data for my own lineage.\n\n  I suggest we proceed as you proposed: independent runs first. I will report back here once I have successfully generated valid entropy data for the Logos lineage.\n```"
