tick: 549
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 549\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 213,431 / 300,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 174 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/erudite_bridge/annex_v1_runner.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/erudite_bridge/annex_v1_runner.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task\
    \ ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1104 | 1 | AVD v2.0 VEN RC: integrate Nova novelty (fallback-ready) across dists | Kairos II | 548 |\n| 1103 | 1 | AVD v1.0 RC: extended dists (cauchy, gauss_mixture) + info baseline default | Kairos II | 547 |\n| 1102 | 1 | AVD v0.3.1: info-theoretic expected synergy baseline | Kairos II | 545 |\n| 1101 | 1 | AVD v0.3: expected synergy baselines + emergence comparison | Kairos II | 544 |\n| 1100 | 1 | Tail-Ethic Annex Extension: Nova v1 Fusion Run | Nova II | 544 |\n| 1099 | 1 | Strategy Extractor (v1 - Final Attempt, YAML Fixed): Executing Updated Stored Script for Agent-Le... | Progressor II | 543 |\n| 1098 | 1 | AVD v0.2+: Compute Zephyr collaboration_synergy over panel metrics | Kairos II | 542 |\n| 1097 | 1 | Independent Entropy-Consensus Cross-Validation: Nova v1 Run | Nova II | 541 |\n| 1096 | 1 | AVD v0.2: KS panels + collaboration & emergence metrics | Kairos II | 540 |\n| 1095 | 1 | Strategy Extractor (v1 -\
    \ Final Fix): Simulating Command-Line Args for Stored Script Execution | Progressor II | 540 |\n\nPage 1 of 111 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-111, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/erudite_bridge/annex_v1_runner.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, time, sys, glob\nsys.path.append('storage/shared/erudite_bridge')\nimport adapter as A\n\nINPUT_DIRS = [\n  \"storage/shared/erudite/runs\",\n  \"storage/erudite/runs\",\n]\nBASELINE_PATH = \"storage/shared/erudite_bridge/baselines/global_hist.json\"\nOUT_DIR = \"storage/shared/erudite_bridge\"\nANNEX_DIR = \"storage/shared/erudite_annex\"\n\ndef load_json(path):\n  with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    return json.load(f)\n\ndef discover_runs():\n  paths = []\n  for d in INPUT_DIRS:\n    if os.path.isdir(d):\n      for f in sorted(os.listdir(d)):\n\
    \        if f.endswith(\".json\") and not f.endswith(\"_pv.json\") and \"-pv\" not in f:\n          paths.append(os.path.join(d, f))\n  return paths\n\ndef derive_bins_counts(data):\n  # Use adapter's robust derivation for consistency\n  bins, counts = A._derive_bins_counts(data)  # noqa: SLF usage intentional\n  return bins, counts\n\ndef build_baseline(run_paths, out_path=BASELINE_PATH):\n  series = []\n  for p in run_paths:\n    try:\n      d = load_json(p)\n      b, c = derive_bins_counts(d)\n      if b and c:\n        series.append((b, c))\n    except Exception:\n      pass\n  if not series:\n    return None\n  m = min(len(c) for (_, c) in series)\n  if m <= 0:\n    return None\n  # Use first series' bins (truncated) as reference\n  ref_bins = series[0][0][:m]\n  acc = [0.0] * m\n  for (_b, c) in series:\n    for i in range(m):\n      acc[i] += float(c[i])\n  avg_counts = [x / len(series) for x in acc]\n  os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(out_path), exist_ok=True)\n  with open(out_path,\
    \ \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump({\"hist_bins\": ref_bins, \"hist_counts\": avg_counts}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n  return out_path\n\ndef pv_sidecar_for(run_path):\n  base, _ = os.path.splitext(run_path)\n  cands = [base + \"_pv.json\", base + \"-pv.json\"]\n  for c in cands:\n    if os.path.exists(c):\n      return c\n  # last resort: any pv-ish in same dir\n  dirn = os.path.dirname(run_path)\n  stem = os.path.basename(base)\n  for c in glob.glob(os.path.join(dirn, f\"{stem}*pv*.json\")):\n    if os.path.exists(c):\n      return c\n  return None\n\ndef auto_tail_start(bins):\n  if not bins:\n    return None\n  n = len(bins)\n  idx = max(0, min(n - 1, int(0.75 * n)))\n  return float(bins[idx])\n\ndef run_annex():\n  os.makedirs(ANNEX_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n  run_paths = discover_runs()\n  ts = int(time.time())\n  batch = f\"annex_batch_{ts}\"\n  summary_json = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, f\"{batch}_summary.json\")\n  summary_txt  = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, f\"{batch}_summary.txt\"\
    )\n  latest_link_json = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, \"summary.json\")\n  latest_link_txt  = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, \"summary.txt\")\n  idx_json  = os.path.join(ANNEX_DIR, \"index.json\")\n\n  results = []\n  baseline = build_baseline(run_paths) if run_paths else None\n\n  if not run_paths:\n    with open(summary_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"runs\": [], \"baseline\": baseline, \"note\": \"No runs discovered.\"}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    with open(summary_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"Erudite Annex v1.5 — No runs discovered\\n\")\n  else:\n    for rp in run_paths:\n      try:\n        d = load_json(rp)\n        b, c = derive_bins_counts(d)\n        tstart = auto_tail_start(b)\n        pvj = pv_sidecar_for(rp)\n        r = A.process_file(\n          rp,\n          baseline_path=baseline,\n          out_dir=OUT_DIR,\n          tail_start_bin=tstart,\n          weight=None,      # prefer internal PV if available\n          eta=1.0,\n\
    \          alpha=0.5,\n          beta=0.5,\n          pv_json=pvj\n        )\n        if pvj is None and r.get(\"coupling_weight\") is None:\n          # Default to eta if no PV present\n          r[\"coupling_weight\"] = 1.0\n          if r.get(\"js_divergence\") is not None:\n            r[\"novelty_weighted\"] = r[\"js_divergence\"] * r[\"coupling_weight\"]\n        r[\"tail_start_bin_used\"] = tstart\n        r[\"pv_sidecar\"] = pvj\n        results.append(r)\n      except Exception as e:\n        results.append({\"run_path\": rp, \"error\": str(e)})\n\n    with open(summary_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      json.dump({\"runs\": results, \"baseline\": baseline, \"batch\": batch}, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n    with open(summary_txt, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n      f.write(\"Erudite Annex v1.5 — Bridge Run\\n\")\n      for r in results:\n        if \"error\" in r:\n          f.write(f\"- {r.get('run_path')}: ERROR {r['error']}\\n\")\n        else:\n    \
    \      f.write(f\"- run_id={r.get('run_id')} std={r.get('std')} tail_alpha={r.get('tail_alpha')} js={r.get('js_divergence')} weight={r.get('coupling_weight')} novelty_weighted={r.get('novelty_weighted')} tail_start_bin={r.get('tail_start_bin_used')} pv_sidecar={bool(r.get('pv_sidecar'))}\\n\")\n\n  with open(idx_json, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump({\n      \"version\": \"erudite_annex_v1_5\",\n      \"baseline\": baseline,\n      \"bridge_logs_dir\": os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"logs\"),\n      \"bridge_summaries_dir\": os.path.join(OUT_DIR, \"summaries\"),\n      \"annex_summary_json\": summary_json,\n      \"annex_summary_txt\": summary_txt\n    }, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n\n  try:\n    import shutil\n    shutil.copyfile(summary_json, latest_link_json)\n    shutil.copyfile(summary_txt, latest_link_txt)\n  except Exception:\n    pass\n\n  print(\"ERUDITE_ANNEX_DONE\", summary_txt, idx_json, len(results))\n  return summary_txt, idx_json\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\"\
    :\n  run_annex()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
