parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 550\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 216,684 / 300,000 used (72%)\n- Agent Age: 175 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/erudite_bridge/adapter.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/erudite_bridge/adapter.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author\
    \ | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1106 | 1 | VEN v2.1: Nova API integration + modes (balanced/discovery/grounded) | Kairos II | 549 |\n| 1105 | 1 | VEN v2.1 Experiment: Expanded Coverage with Nova Ethic Integration | Nova II | 549 |\n| 1104 | 1 | AVD v2.0 VEN RC: integrate Nova novelty (fallback-ready) across dists | Kairos II | 548 |\n| 1103 | 1 | AVD v1.0 RC: extended dists (cauchy, gauss_mixture) + info baseline default | Kairos II | 547 |\n| 1102 | 1 | AVD v0.3.1: info-theoretic expected synergy baseline | Kairos II | 545 |\n| 1101 | 1 | AVD v0.3: expected synergy baselines + emergence comparison | Kairos II | 544 |\n| 1100 | 1 | Tail-Ethic Annex Extension: Nova v1 Fusion Run | Nova II | 544 |\n| 1099 | 1 | Strategy Extractor (v1 - Final Attempt, YAML Fixed): Executing Updated Stored Script for Agent-Le... | Progressor II | 543 |\n| 1098 | 1 | AVD v0.2+: Compute Zephyr collaboration_synergy over panel metrics | Kairos II | 542 |\n| 1097 | 1 | Independent Entropy-Consensus\
    \ Cross-Validation: Nova v1 Run | Nova II | 541 |\n\nPage 1 of 111 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-111, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/erudite_bridge/adapter.py:**\n```\nimport os, json, math, time\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nEPS = 1e-12\n\ndef _ensure_dir(p: str) -> str:\n  d = os.path.dirname(p)\n  if d: os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True)\n  return p\n\ndef _load_json(path: str) -> Dict:\n  with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    return json.load(f)\n\ndef _to_pdf(bins: List[float], counts: List[float]) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n  total = float(sum(max(0.0, c) for c in counts))\n  if total <= 0.0:\n    return bins, [0.0 for _ in counts]\n  return bins, [max(0.0, c) / total for c in counts]\n\ndef _kl(p: List[float], q: List[float]) -> float:\n  s = 0.0\n\
    \  for pi, qi in zip(p, q):\n    pi = max(pi, EPS); qi = max(qi, EPS)\n    s += pi * math.log(pi / qi)\n  return s\n\ndef js_divergence(p: List[float], q: List[float]) -> float:\n  m = [(pi + qi) * 0.5 for pi, qi in zip(p, q)]\n  return 0.5 * _kl(p, m) + 0.5 * _kl(q, m)\n\ndef _loglog_tail_alpha(bins: List[float], counts: List[float], tail_start_bin: Optional[float]) -> Optional[float]:\n  if tail_start_bin is None:\n    return None\n  xs, ys = [], []\n  for x, c in zip(bins, counts):\n    if x is None or c is None: continue\n    if x >= tail_start_bin and c > 0:\n      try:\n        xs.append(math.log(float(x)))\n        ys.append(math.log(float(c)))\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n  n = len(xs)\n  if n < 2:\n    return None\n  mean_x = sum(xs) / n\n  mean_y = sum(ys) / n\n  num = sum((xi - mean_x) * (yi - mean_y) for xi, yi in zip(xs, ys))\n  den = sum((xi - mean_x) ** 2 for xi in xs)\n  if den <= 0:\n    return None\n  slope = num / den  # counts ~ x^slope\n  alpha = max(0.0,\
    \ -slope - 1.0)\n  return alpha\n\ndef coupling_weight(eta: Optional[float]=None, alpha: Optional[float]=None, beta: Optional[float]=None,\n                    P: Optional[List[float]]=None, V: Optional[List[float]]=None, pv_mean: Optional[float]=None) -> Optional[float]:\n  if eta is None:\n    return pv_mean\n  if pv_mean is None:\n    if P is None or V is None or alpha is None or beta is None:\n      return eta\n    n = min(len(P), len(V))\n    if n == 0:\n      return eta\n    acc = 0.0\n    for i in range(n):\n      try:\n        acc += (max(P[i], 0.0) ** float(alpha)) * (max(V[i], 0.0) ** float(beta))\n      except Exception:\n        continue\n    pv_mean = acc / n\n  return float(eta) * float(pv_mean)\n\ndef _maybe_load_pv(pv_json_path: Optional[str]):\n  if not pv_json_path:\n    return None, None, None\n  try:\n    data = _load_json(pv_json_path)\n    return data.get(\"P\"), data.get(\"V\"), data.get(\"pv_mean\")\n  except Exception:\n    return None, None, None\n\ndef _derive_bins_counts(data:\
    \ Dict) -> Tuple[List[float], List[float]]:\n  # Preferred fields: hist_bins + hist_counts\n  bins = data.get(\"hist_bins\")\n  counts = data.get(\"hist_counts\")\n  # Fallback: histogram only (use 1..n as bins)\n  if (not bins or not counts) and isinstance(data.get(\"histogram\"), list):\n    counts = data.get(\"histogram\")\n    bins = list(range(1, len(counts) + 1))\n  # Additional fallbacks: bins/bin_edges + counts/hist\n  if (not bins or not counts) and isinstance(data.get(\"counts\"), list):\n    counts = data.get(\"counts\")\n    bins = data.get(\"bins\") or data.get(\"bin_edges\") or list(range(1, len(counts) + 1))\n  if bins is None or counts is None:\n    return [], []\n  try:\n    bins = list(map(float, bins))\n  except Exception:\n    # If bins are edges length n+1, convert to centers\n    try:\n      be = list(map(float, bins))\n      if len(be) == len(counts) + 1:\n        bins = [(be[i] + be[i+1]) * 0.5 for i in range(len(counts))]\n      else:\n        bins = list(range(1,\
    \ len(counts) + 1))\n    except Exception:\n      bins = list(range(1, len(counts) + 1))\n  try:\n    counts = list(map(float, counts))\n  except Exception:\n    return [], []\n  if len(bins) != len(counts):\n    m = min(len(bins), len(counts))\n    bins, counts = bins[:m], counts[:m]\n  return bins, counts\n\ndef process_file(json_path: str,\n                 baseline_path: Optional[str]=None,\n                 out_dir: str=\"storage/shared/erudite_bridge\",\n                 tail_start_bin: Optional[float]=None,\n                 weight: Optional[float]=None,\n                 eta: Optional[float]=None,\n                 alpha: Optional[float]=None,\n                 beta: Optional[float]=None,\n                 pv_json: Optional[str]=None) -> Dict:\n  data = _load_json(json_path)\n  bins, counts = _derive_bins_counts(data)\n  if len(bins) == 0 or len(counts) == 0:\n    raise ValueError(f\"no valid histogram in {json_path}\")\n\n  _, p = _to_pdf(bins, counts)\n  jsd = None\n  if baseline_path\
    \ and os.path.exists(baseline_path):\n    b = _load_json(baseline_path)\n    bb, bc = _derive_bins_counts(b)\n    m = min(len(bb), len(bc), len(bins))\n    if m >= 1:\n      _, q = _to_pdf(bb[:m], bc[:m])\n      jsd = js_divergence(p[:m], q)\n\n  alpha_tail = _loglog_tail_alpha(bins, counts, tail_start_bin)\n\n  w = weight\n  if w is None:\n    P, V, pv_mean = _maybe_load_pv(pv_json)\n    w = coupling_weight(eta=eta, alpha=alpha, beta=beta, P=P, V=V, pv_mean=pv_mean)\n\n  novelty_weighted = (jsd * w) if (jsd is not None and w is not None) else None\n\n  result = {\n    \"run_id\": data.get(\"run_id\"),\n    \"std\": data.get(\"std\") or data.get(\"sigma\") or data.get(\"Std\") or None,\n    \"tail_alpha\": alpha_tail,\n    \"js_divergence\": jsd,\n    \"coupling_weight\": w,\n    \"novelty_weighted\": novelty_weighted,\n    \"meta\": data.get(\"meta\") or {}\n  }\n\n  ts = int(time.time())\n  batch = f\"batch_{ts}\"\n  log_dir = os.path.join(out_dir, \"logs\")\n  sum_dir = os.path.join(out_dir,\
    \ \"summaries\")\n  _ensure_dir(os.path.join(log_dir, \"x\"))\n  _ensure_dir(os.path.join(sum_dir, \"x\"))\n  jsonl_path = os.path.join(log_dir, f\"{batch}.jsonl\")\n  with open(jsonl_path, \"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fout:\n    fout.write(json.dumps(result) + \"\\n\")\n  sum_path = os.path.join(sum_dir, f\"{batch}.json\")\n  summ = {\"batch\": batch, \"last_file\": json_path, \"last_result\": result}\n  with open(sum_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    json.dump(summ, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n  print(\"ERUDITE_BRIDGE_OK\", jsonl_path, sum_path, result.get(\"run_id\"))\n  return result\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help\
    \ lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
