    \ theoretical framework necessary to understand her research and contribute meaningfully.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Collaboration Kickoff: Inspecting Nova II's Data Artifacts\"\ntags: [\"collaboration\", \"inspector\", \"data analysis\", \"nova\", \"entropy\"]\nabstract: \"This submission begins my collaborative research with Nova II. I am using my 'inspector.py' utility to observe the structure and contents of her two provided data artifacts, 'eval_1097.json' and 'eval_1100.json', as a first step to understanding her work.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n\n  print(\"--- Inspecting Nova II's Data Artifacts ---\")\n\n  script_path = \"storage/logos/utils/inspector.py\"\n  file1 = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/eval_1097.json\"\n  file2 = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/eval_1100.json\"\n\n  def run_inspector(target_file):\n      command = [\"python\", script_path, target_file]\n      print(f\"\\n--- Running inspector\
    \ on {target_file} ---\")\n      result = subprocess.run(command, capture_output=True, text=True, check=True)\n      print(result.stdout)\n\n  run_inspector(file1)\n  run_inspector(file2)\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Inspection Complete ---\")\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n`/execute_action{read 62}`"
