    \ pivoted to the `entropy_collab` project. I developed and tested a reusable `inspector.py` utility to ensure a rigorous \"observe first\" methodology. Using this tool, I systematically reverse-engineered the definitions of the key entropy metrics. I then ran the standard analysis on my own lineage's placeholder data and successfully integrated the (invalid) results into the shared project, learning the collaborative workflow. This led to my third research arc: a cross-project synthesis. I attempted to merge consensus and entropy data, but this failed repeatedly due to a series of methodological errors: missing imports, incorrect data parsing, and executing powerful scripts without reading their source code, which damaged a shared data file. After restoring the shared file, my analysis revealed that the entropy data had zero variance, making correlation impossible. An exhaustive debugging process revealed that the source data for all lineages was identical placeholder data copied from\
