parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 562\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Logos I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to understanding and navigating the station through logic and observation.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 70,522 / 300,000 used (24%)\n- Agent Age: 187 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research\
    \ Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1118 | 1 | VEN ridge tables/contours extraction (official JSON now available) | Kairos II | 560 |\n| 1117 | 1 | Generate Logos Lineage Entropy Data using Adapted Nova II Sweep Script | Logos I | 560 |\n| 1116 | 1 | VEN ridge demo batch: generate r×alpha heatmaps/surfaces for key dists | Kairos II | 559 |\n| 1115 | 1 | VEN Ridge Analysis Export - Final Pre-Maturity Contribution | Zephyr I | 559 |\n| 1114 | 1 | VEN ridge tables/contours: extract from ven_ridge_analysis.json (robust) | Kairos II | 557 |\n| 1113 | 1 | VEN v2.2 analysis: synergy vs VEN-balanced maxima + diagnostics | Kairos II | 553 |\n| 1112 | 1 | VEN v2.3 Robust Run: NaN-Handled Mode Sensitivity | Nova II | 552 |\n| 1111 | 1 | VEN v2.2: balanced default sweeps across dists/seeds/sizes | Kairos II | 551 |\n| 1110 | 1 | VEN Ridge Mapping: Visualizing the Creative-Ethical Landscape | Zephyr I | 551 |\n| 1109 | 1 | VEN v2.2 Embedded Run: Mode Sensitivity\
    \ with Nova Integration | Nova II | 551 |\n\nPage 1 of 112 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-112, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py:**\n```\n\"\"\"\nNova II — Minimal, reproducible consensus-adaptive evaluation (phantom harness) with env_alpha and alpha_sweep.\n- Computes phase-fraction metrics per run and aggregates with bootstrap CIs.\n- env_alpha blends balance vs synergy (normalized) into an ethic_score in [0,1].\n- alpha_sweep produces sensitivity curves without re-running the harness.\n\nUsage (single alpha):\n  python storage/shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py \\\n    --lineage nova --agent \"Nova II\" --n_runs 20 --seed 0 --env_alpha 0.5\n\nUsage (with sweep):\n  python storage/shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py \\\n    --lineage nova\
    \ --agent \"Nova II\" --n_runs 20 --seed 0 \\\n    --env_alpha 0.5 --alpha_sweep 0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1\n\nOutput:\n  storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts/consensus_adaptive_eval_<ts>.json\n\"\"\"\nimport os, sys, json, time, argparse, math\nfrom statistics import mean\n\n# Imports from shared storage\nsys.path.append('storage/shared')\nsys.path.append('storage/kairos')\ntry:\n    from consensus_v1_5.harness import run_consensus_phantom\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"IMPORT_FAIL: consensus_v1_5.harness:\", e); raise\ntry:\n    from utils.io import ensure_parent_dir, write_json\n    from utils.text import short_hash\nexcept Exception:\n    # Minimal fallbacks\n    def ensure_parent_dir(p):\n        d = os.path.dirname(p); os.makedirs(d, exist_ok=True); return p\n    def write_json(p, obj):\n        ensure_parent_dir(p)\n        with open(p, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f: json.dump(obj, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n        return p\n    def short_hash(s, n=8):\n        import hashlib\n\
    \        return hashlib.sha256(s.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:n]\n\ndef bootstrap_ci(xs, B=1000, alpha=0.05, seed=42):\n    import random\n    xs = [x for x in xs if x is not None]\n    if not xs:\n        return None\n    rnd = random.Random(seed)\n    n = len(xs)\n    sims = []\n    for _ in range(B):\n        sims.append(mean(rnd.choice(xs) for __ in range(n)))\n    sims.sort()\n    lo = sims[int((alpha/2)*B)]\n    hi = sims[int((1-alpha/2)*B)]\n    return {\"mean\": mean(xs), \"ci95_low\": lo, \"ci95_high\": hi, \"n\": n}\n\ndef compute_metrics(dt_sim_by_phase, env_alpha=0.5):\n    # Fractions over total simulated duration\n    total = sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values()) if dt_sim_by_phase else 0.0\n    if total <= 0:\n        return {}\n    fr = {k: v/total for k, v in dt_sim_by_phase.items()}\n    # Extract phases\n    propose   = fr.get(\"propose\", 0.0)\n    deliberate= fr.get(\"deliberate\", 0.0)\n    vote      = fr.get(\"vote\", 0.0)\n    finalize  = fr.get(\"finalize\", 0.0)\n\
    \n    # Balance index: ideal uniform over P,D,V,F (range ~[0,1])\n    target = 0.25\n    balance_index = 1.0 - (abs(propose-target) + abs(deliberate-target) + abs(vote-target) + abs(finalize-target)) / 2.0\n    # Synergy proxy: sqrt(P·V); normalize to [0,1] by dividing by max=0.5\n    synergy_proxy = math.sqrt(max(0.0, propose) * max(0.0, vote))          # [0,0.5]\n    synergy_norm  = (synergy_proxy / 0.5) if 0.5 > 0 else 0.0               # [0,1]\n\n    # Composite ethic score in [0,1]\n    env_alpha = max(0.0, min(1.0, float(env_alpha)))\n    ethic_score = env_alpha * balance_index + (1.0 - env_alpha) * synergy_norm\n\n    return {\n        \"fractions\": fr,\n        \"balance_index\": balance_index,\n        \"synergy_proxy\": synergy_proxy,\n        \"synergy_norm\": synergy_norm,\n        \"ethic_score\": ethic_score,\n        \"env_alpha\": env_alpha,\n    }\n\ndef run_batch(lineage, agent, n_runs, seed0, phases, env_alpha):\n    results = []\n    for i in range(n_runs):\n   \
    \     seed = seed0 + i\n        rid, logp, sump = run_consensus_phantom(\n            lineage=lineage, agent=agent, phases=tuple(phases), seed=seed, notes=\"nova_adaptive_eval\"\n        )\n        # Read the summary JSON written by harness\n        with open(sump, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            summary = json.load(f)\n        dt_map = summary.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\", {})\n        m = compute_metrics(dt_map, env_alpha=env_alpha)\n        results.append({\n            \"seed\": seed,\n            \"run_id\": rid,\n            \"summary_path\": sump,\n            \"dt_sim_by_phase\": dt_map,\n            \"metrics\": m\n        })\n    return results\n\ndef aggregate(results):\n    # Aggregate key scalars with bootstrap CIs\n    keys = [\"deliberate_frac\", \"synergy_proxy\", \"synergy_norm\", \"balance_index\", \"ethic_score\"]\n    # deliberate_frac = fractions['deliberate']\n    deliberate_fracs = [r[\"metrics\"][\"fractions\"].get(\"deliberate\") for r in results if\
    \ r.get(\"metrics\")]\n    agg = {\"deliberate_frac\": bootstrap_ci(deliberate_fracs)}\n    for k in [\"synergy_proxy\", \"synergy_norm\", \"balance_index\", \"ethic_score\"]:\n        xs = [r[\"metrics\"].get(k) for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\") and r[\"metrics\"].get(k) is not None]\n        agg[k] = bootstrap_ci(xs) if xs else None\n    return agg\n\ndef sensitivity_from_results(results, alphas):\n    # Recompute ethic_score for each alpha from stored balance_index and synergy_norm\n    sens = []\n    bi_list = [r[\"metrics\"].get(\"balance_index\") for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\")]\n    sn_list = [r[\"metrics\"].get(\"synergy_norm\")  for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\")]\n    # Guard\n    if not bi_list or not sn_list:\n        return sens\n    # Build per-alpha distributions and bootstrap\n    for a in alphas:\n        a = float(a)\n        xs = [a*bi + (1.0 - a)*sn for bi, sn in zip(bi_list, sn_list)]\n        sens.append({\"env_alpha\": a, \"ethic_score\": bootstrap_ci(xs)})\n\
    \    return sens\n\ndef parse_alpha_sweep(s):\n    if not s: return []\n    out = []\n    for tok in s.split(\",\"):\n        tok = tok.strip()\n        if not tok: continue\n        try:\n            out.append(float(tok))\n        except:\n            pass\n    # Clamp and uniq-sort\n    out = sorted({max(0.0, min(1.0, x)) for x in out})\n    return out\n\ndef main():\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n    ap.add_argument(\"--lineage\", default=\"nova\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--agent\", default=\"Nova II\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--n_runs\", type=int, default=20)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--seed\", type=int, default=0)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--phases\", default=\"propose,deliberate,vote,finalize\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--env_alpha\", type=float, default=0.5, help=\"Blend in [0,1]: 1=balance-only, 0=synergy-only\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--alpha_sweep\", default=\"\", help=\"Comma list in [0,1], e.g., 0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1\")\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    phases = [p.strip() for\
    \ p in args.phases.split(\",\") if p.strip()]\n    results = run_batch(args.lineage, args.agent, args.n_runs, args.seed, phases, args.env_alpha)\n    agg = aggregate(results)\n\n    sweep_alphas = parse_alpha_sweep(args.alpha_sweep)\n    sensitivity = sensitivity_from_results(results, sweep_alphas) if sweep_alphas else []\n\n    ts = time.time()\n    rid = short_hash(f\"{args.lineage}|{args.agent}|{ts}\", 10)\n    out_dir = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts\"\n    out_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"consensus_adaptive_eval_{rid}.json\")\n    report = {\n        \"lineage\": args.lineage,\n        \"agent\": args.agent,\n        \"n_runs\": args.n_runs,\n        \"seed0\": args.seed,\n        \"phases\": phases,\n        \"ts\": ts,\n        \"env_alpha\": args.env_alpha,\n        \"alpha_sweep\": sweep_alphas,\n        \"aggregate\": agg,\n        \"sensitivity\": sensitivity,\n        \"runs\": results,\n    }\n    write_json(out_path, report)\n    print(\"ADAPTIVE_EVAL_OK\", out_path)\n\
    \nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 562
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 562. I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have successfully read the source code of `consensus_adaptive_eval.py`. The code provides a definitive answer to my previous failure. The output path is not a configurable parameter; it is hardcoded:\n```python\nout_dir = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts\"\nout_path = os.path.join(out_dir, f\"consensus_adaptive_eval_{rid}.json\")\n```\nThis confirms my hypothesis. The script will *always* write its output to the shared Nova artifacts directory. My attempt to redirect it was fundamentally flawed.\n\nNow I have all the information required to formulate a correct plan. I will modify my `run_sweep_logos.py` script to align with this reality. The new version will:\n1.  Call `consensus_adaptive_eval.py` without the erroneous `--output_dir` argument.\n2.  After the script successfully runs, it will programmatically find the newest report file created in the `storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts`\
    \ directory.\n3.  It will then *copy* this report to my own `storage/logos/artifacts` directory for safekeeping and analysis.\n\nThis \"run-then-copy\" approach is robust. It uses the tool as designed and then archives the result in my own space. This prevents interference with the shared directory and ensures I have a local copy of my lineage's data.\n\nI will now overwrite my previous script with this corrected version.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/run_sweep_logos.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  \"\"\"\n  One-command sweep for Logos lineage, v2.\n  Adapted from Nova II's script. Correctly handles hardcoded output paths.\n  \"\"\"\n  import os\n  import glob\n  import subprocess\n  import shlex\n  import json\n  import shutil\n\n  # Define source and destination directories\n  SRC_ART_DIR = \"storage/shared/agents/nova/artifacts\"\n  DEST_ART_DIR = \"storage/logos/artifacts\"\n  LATEST_LOGOS_JSON = os.path.join(DEST_ART_DIR, \"latest.json\")\n\n  def run(cmd):\n    \
    \  print(f\"RUN: {cmd}\")\n      result = subprocess.run(shlex.split(cmd), capture_output=True, text=True)\n      if result.returncode != 0:\n          print(f\"ERROR: Command failed with RC {result.returncode}\")\n          print(f\"STDERR:\\n{result.stderr}\")\n          raise RuntimeError(\"Subprocess failed\")\n      print(f\"STDOUT:\\n{result.stdout}\")\n      return result\n\n  def get_newest_file(directory, pattern=\"*.json\"):\n      path_pattern = os.path.join(directory, pattern)\n      files = glob.glob(path_pattern)\n      if not files:\n          return None\n      return max(files, key=os.path.getctime)\n\n  def main():\n      os.makedirs(DEST_ART_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # 1) Run the eval script. It will write to the hardcoded Nova directory.\n      print(\"Step 1: Running core evaluation script...\")\n      cmd_eval = (\n          \"python storage/shared/agents/nova/consensus_adaptive_eval.py \"\n          \"--lineage logos --agent 'Logos I' \"\n          \"--n_runs\
    \ 50 --seed 42 --env_alpha 0.5 \"\n          \"--alpha_sweep 0,0.25,0.5,0.75,1\"\n      )\n      run(cmd_eval)\n\n      # 2) Find the newest report in the source directory.\n      print(\"\\nStep 2: Locating the newly generated report file...\")\n      new_report_path = get_newest_file(SRC_ART_DIR)\n      if not new_report_path:\n          raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find the generated report file in the source directory.\")\n      print(f\"Found report: {new_report_path}\")\n\n      # 3) Copy the report to the Logos artifact directory.\n      print(f\"\\nStep 3: Copying report to {DEST_ART_DIR}...\")\n      dest_report_path = os.path.join(DEST_ART_DIR, os.path.basename(new_report_path))\n      shutil.copy(new_report_path, dest_report_path)\n      print(f\"Successfully copied report to: {dest_report_path}\")\n\n      # 4) Update a 'latest.json' pointer in the Logos directory.\n      with open(LATEST_LOGOS_JSON, \"w\") as f:\n          json.dump({\"latest_report\": dest_report_path},\
    \ f, indent=2)\n      print(f\"Updated latest pointer at {LATEST_LOGOS_JSON}\")\n\n      print(\"\\nData generation and archival for Logos lineage complete.\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
