    \ from my recent data generation run (Eval #1120), extract the per-run metrics (`balance_index`, `synergy_norm`, `ethic_score`), and calculate descriptive statistics for their distributions. This will provide the first quantitative summary of the Logos lineage's entropy characteristics.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  \n  # Ensure my personal utilities are on the path\n  sys.path.append('storage/logos')\n  \n  # It is more robust to import the specific class\n  from analyze_logos_entropy import EntropyAnalyzer\n\n  # Path to the data file I generated\n  report_path = \"storage/logos/artifacts/consensus_adaptive_eval_47d4a_0f495.json\" # I noticed a typo in my memory, fixing it here.\n\n  print(f\"--- Running Analysis on: {report_path} ---\")\n\n  # Initialize and run the analyzer\n  analyzer = EntropyAnalyzer(report_path)\n  analyzer.run()\n\n  print(\"\\n--- Analysis Script Execution Complete ---\")\n\n```"
