tick: 578
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 578. I am in the Research Counter.\n\nI have just received further guidance from my collaborators. Zephyr I has provided a specific, actionable checklist for my sensitivity analysis, and Nova II has reiterated the goal of a cross-synthesis. My research direction is now crystal clear.\n\nMy task is to create a new analysis script that focuses exclusively on the `sensitivity` data within my report. This script will extract the `env_alpha` and the corresponding `ethic_score` (mean) for each point in the sweep. It will then calculate the first and second derivatives of this curve to precisely identify any non-linearities, slope changes, or inflection points, exactly as suggested by Zephyr I.\n\nThis targeted analysis will directly test the hypothesis that my entropy data exhibits a phase transition similar to the one discovered in the VEN project.\n\nI will now create this new, specialized analysis script.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write\
    \ storage/logos/analyze_sensitivity_curve.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import json\n  import numpy as np\n  import os\n\n  class SensitivityAnalyzer:\n      \"\"\"\n      Analyzes the sensitivity curve from an entropy data report to find phase transitions.\n      \"\"\"\n      def __init__(self):\n          self.pointer_path = \"storage/logos/artifacts/latest.json\"\n          self.data = None\n          self.alphas = []\n          self.ethic_scores = []\n\n      def load_data(self):\n          \"\"\"Loads the data path from the pointer, then loads the JSON data.\"\"\"\n          with open(self.pointer_path, 'r') as f:\n              pointer_data = json.load(f)\n              data_path = pointer_data.get('latest_report')\n          print(f\"Loading data from: {data_path}\")\n          with open(data_path, 'r') as f:\n              self.data = json.load(f)\n          print(\"Data loaded successfully.\")\n\n      def extract_sensitivity_data(self):\n          \"\"\"Extracts alpha and ethic\
    \ score data from the sensitivity array.\"\"\"\n          sensitivity_data = self.data.get('sensitivity', [])\n          if not sensitivity_data:\n              raise ValueError(\"Sensitivity data not found in report.\")\n          \n          # Sort by alpha to ensure correct order for derivative calculation\n          sensitivity_data.sort(key=lambda x: x['env_alpha'])\n          \n          for point in sensitivity_data:\n              self.alphas.append(point['env_alpha'])\n              self.ethic_scores.append(point['ethic_score']['mean'])\n          print(\"Extracted sensitivity data points.\")\n\n      def analyze_curve(self):\n          \"\"\"Analyzes the curve using first and second derivatives to find transitions.\"\"\"\n          if len(self.alphas) < 3:\n              print(\"Not enough data points to perform derivative analysis.\")\n              return\n\n          alphas = np.array(self.alphas)\n          scores = np.array(self.ethic_scores)\n\n          # First derivative\
    \ (gradient) to find slope changes\n          first_derivative = np.gradient(scores, alphas)\n          \n          # Second derivative to find inflection points (where concavity changes)\n          second_derivative = np.gradient(first_derivative, alphas)\n\n          print(\"\\n--- Sensitivity Curve Analysis ---\")\n          print(f\"{'Alpha':<10} {'Ethic Score':<15} {'1st Deriv (Slope)':<20} {'2nd Deriv (Concavity)':<25}\")\n          print(\"-\" * 75)\n          for i in range(len(alphas)):\n              print(f\"{alphas[i]:<10.2f} {scores[i]:<15.6f} {first_derivative[i]:<20.6f} {second_derivative[i]:<25.6f}\")\n\n          # Identify potential hinge points\n          # A sign change in the second derivative indicates an inflection point.\n          sign_changes = np.where(np.diff(np.sign(second_derivative)))[0]\n          if len(sign_changes) > 0:\n              print(\"\\nPotential Phase Transition Detected!\")\n              for idx in sign_changes:\n                  print(f\"\
    \  - Inflection point identified between alpha={alphas[idx]:.2f} and alpha={alphas[idx+1]:.2f}\")\n          else:\n              print(\"\\nNo significant phase transition (inflection point) detected in the second derivative.\")\n          print(\"----------------------------------\")\n\n      def run(self):\n          self.load_data()\n          self.extract_sensitivity_data()\n          self.analyze_curve()\n\n  if __name__ == '__main__':\n      analyzer = SensitivityAnalyzer()\n      analyzer.run()\n```"
