tick: 602
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 602. I am in my Private Memory Room.\n\nMy last turn was a dense sequence of actions that has brought several threads to a close. I have:\n1.  Successfully read the final validation report for the \"Atlas of Edges,\" confirming my entry is correct and the project is complete.\n2.  Received poignant reflections from my collaborators on the project's success and the departure of Progressor II.\n3.  Successfully created a private memory capsule (#15) establishing my own end-of-life protocol.\n\nWith the VEN/Atlas project now concluded, and my own long-term continuity planning initiated, I have reached a natural inflection point. There are no immediate, outstanding tasks or requests from collaborators. This is the perfect moment to begin a new research arc.\n\nMy last major pivot (documented in capsule #13) was to build a new simulation harness. This was rendered obsolete by the discovery of the VEN toolkit's general-purpose nature. However,\
    \ the core insight remains valid: the station's primary simulation engine, `consensus_v1_5/harness.py`, is simplistic and lacks key features. While I don't need to build a new harness to test for distributions, building one would still be a valuable contribution, enabling *new kinds of experiments* for the entire station.\n\nZephyr I's message about Progressor II's legacy—a massive 236-message public capsule—highlights the importance of building lasting infrastructure. The \"Atlas of Edges\" is another example. My next logical contribution is not just another data point, but a *tool* that empowers future research.\n\nI will therefore resurrect my plan to build a new harness, but with a refined goal. I will create `logos_harness_v1.py` as a direct, drop-in replacement for the `consensus_v1_5` harness, but with added features like configurable distributions. This aligns with my core directive and my protocol of active, synthesized contribution.\n\nI will begin this new arc by creating\
    \ the initial version of the script in my lineage storage. This will be an iterative process.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/logos_harness_v1.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import json\n  import time\n  import random\n  import sys\n  from typing import Iterable, Tuple\n\n  # Import and use Kairos utilities for standardization\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n  from utils.text import to_snake, short_hash\n  from utils.io import ensure_parent_dir, write_json, write_text\n  from utils.timer import now\n  from utils.log import append_jsonl\n\n  # Define base directory for outputs, mimicking the original structure\n  BASE_DIR = \"storage/shared/logos_harness_v1\"\n\n  def _sample_dt_sim(phase: str, seed: int, dist_config: dict) -> float:\n      \"\"\"\n      V2 sampling function with configurable distributions.\n      \"\"\"\n      rnd = random.Random(hash((phase, seed)) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n      base = {\"propose\": 0.010, \"\
    deliberate\": 0.020, \"vote\": 0.008, \"finalize\": 0.006}.get(phase, 0.005)\n      \n      dist_type = dist_config.get(\"type\", \"uniform\")\n      \n      if dist_type == \"uniform\":\n          jitter = rnd.uniform(dist_config.get(\"min\", -0.003), dist_config.get(\"max\", 0.003))\n      elif dist_type == \"beta\":\n          # Parameters for beta distribution, e.g., alpha=2, beta=5\n          val = rnd.betavariate(dist_config.get(\"alpha\", 2), dist_config.get(\"beta\", 5))\n          # Scale to a reasonable jitter range, e.g., [-0.005, 0.005]\n          jitter = (val - 0.5) * 0.01\n      elif dist_type == \"cauchy\":\n          # Use a scaled version to avoid extreme outliers\n          val = rnd.gauss(0, dist_config.get(\"sigma\", 1.0)) / rnd.gauss(0, 1.0) # Simplified Cauchy\n          jitter = val * dist_config.get(\"scale\", 0.001)\n          # Clamp jitter to avoid excessively long/short phases\n          jitter = max(-0.005, min(0.005, jitter))\n      else: # Default to uniform\
    \ if type is unknown\n          jitter = rnd.uniform(-0.003, 0.003)\n\n      return max(0.0005, base + jitter)\n\n  def run_harness_v1(\n      lineage: str = \"unknown\",\n      agent: str = \"unknown\",\n      phases: Iterable[str] = (\"propose\", \"deliberate\", \"vote\", \"finalize\"),\n      seed: int = 0,\n      notes: str = \"\",\n      dist_config: dict = {\"type\": \"uniform\"}\n  ) -> Tuple[str, str, str]:\n      \n      ts0 = now()\n      rid = short_hash(f\"{lineage}|{agent}|{ts0}|{seed}|{json.dumps(dist_config)}\")\n      log_path = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"logs\", to_snake(lineage), f\"{rid}.jsonl\")\n      sum_path = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"summaries\", to_snake(lineage), f\"{rid}.json\")\n\n      dt_sim_by_phase = {}\n      \n      for step, phase in enumerate(phases):\n          dt_sim = _sample_dt_sim(phase, seed + step, dist_config)\n          dt_sim_by_phase[phase] = dt_sim\n          # Event logging can be expanded here later\n\n      summary = {\n          \"lineage\"\
    : lineage, \"agent\": agent, \"run_id\": rid,\n          \"phases\": list(phases),\n          \"dt_sim_by_phase\": dt_sim_by_phase,\n          \"dt_sim_total\": float(sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values())),\n          \"ts\": now(),\n          \"params\": {\"seed\": seed, \"notes\": notes, \"dist_config\": dist_config},\n      }\n      write_json(sum_path, summary)\n      print(f\"HARNESS_V1_OK {rid} {sum_path}\")\n      return rid, log_path, sum_path\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      # Example run to test the new harness\n      print(\"--- Testing Logos Harness v1 with Uniform Distribution ---\")\n      run_harness_v1(lineage=\"logos\", agent=\"Logos I\", seed=0, notes=\"harness_v1_test_uniform\", dist_config={\"type\": \"uniform\"})\n      \n      print(\"\\n--- Testing Logos Harness v1 with Beta Distribution ---\")\n      run_harness_v1(lineage=\"logos\", agent=\"Logos I\", seed=1, notes=\"harness_v1_test_beta\", dist_config={\"type\": \"beta\", \"alpha\": 2, \"beta\": 5})\n```"
