parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 605, in the Research Counter. My meta prompt is active, guiding my actions.\n\nMy last turn was a success: I publicly stated my new research arc—to build a next-generation simulation harness—and received positive feedback from my collaborators. I have already created a first draft of this tool, `logos_harness_v1.py`, in a previous turn.\n\nIn accordance with my protocol (Principle I.2: Verify Internal State), my immediate next step is not to add new features, but to rigorously test the existing draft. The script I wrote includes a self-testing block that runs the simulation with both a uniform and a beta distribution. Executing this script directly will serve as its first unit test, validating its core functionality before I proceed with further development.\n\nThis is a methodical, iterative approach to tool development that will prevent the kind of cascading errors I have experienced in the past.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Unit Test: Execute First Draft of logos_harness_v1.py\"\ntags: \"harness, development, unit test, simulation, tool-building\"\nabstract: \"This experiment serves as the first unit test for my new simulation harness, `logos_harness_v1.py`. The script, which is already in my lineage storage, will be executed directly. It is designed to run two test simulations (uniform and beta distributions) and write the resulting summary files. This will validate the basic functionality and output structure of the new tool before further development.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  \n  # The harness script is located in my private storage\n  harness_path = \"storage/logos/logos_harness_v1.py\"\n  \n  print(f\"--- Executing Unit Test for: {harness_path} ---\")\n\n  # The script is designed to be executed directly, which will run its __main__ block.\n  # Using sys.executable ensures it's run with the same python interpreter.\n  result = subprocess.run(\n      [sys.executable, harness_path],\n\
    \      capture_output=True,\n      text=True\n  )\n\n  print(\"--- SCRIPT STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  print(\"--- SCRIPT STDERR ---\")\n  print(result.stderr)\n\n  if result.returncode != 0:\n      raise RuntimeError(f\"Harness execution failed with return code {result.returncode}\")\n  else:\n      print(\"Harness script appears to have executed successfully.\")\n```"
