- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 609, in the Research Counter. My meta prompt is active.\n\nI have just performed the verification step that I have repeatedly failed to do. The file listings for `kairos/` and `kairos/utils/` provide the definitive answer to my import problem.\n\n**Analysis of Findings:**\n*   `storage/kairos/utils/` **does** contain an `__init__.py` file.\n*   The `ModuleNotFoundError` was therefore not because `utils` isn't a package, but because the parent directory, `storage/kairos`, was not on the `sys.path`.\n*   My previous fix, `sys.path.append('storage/kairos')`, was correct in theory, but it must have been executed *after* the import statement was attempted. Python evaluates imports at the top of a file.\n\nThe logical error was subtle: it was the *order* of operations within my script, not the content of the `sys.path.append` line itself.\n\nI now have a clear, precise, and verified path to a solution. I will correct the `logos_harness_v1.py`\
    \ script one last time, ensuring that the `sys.path.append` statements are at the very top of the script, *before* any other imports are attempted. This will guarantee that the interpreter can find the necessary packages.\n\nWith my collaborators making rapid progress, this must be my final attempt at a unit test. Adherence to my protocol has led me to this correct diagnosis, and it must now lead me to a successful execution.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/logos_harness_v1.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # CORRECTED v4: sys.path modifications must be the VERY FIRST thing.\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/shared')\n  sys.path.append('storage/kairos')\n\n  import os\n  import json\n  import time\n  import random\n  from typing import Iterable, Tuple\n\n  from utils.text import to_snake, short_hash\n  from utils.io import ensure_parent_dir, write_json\n  from utils.timer import now\n  \n  BASE_DIR = \"storage/shared/logos_harness_v1\"\n\n  def _sample_dt_sim(phase:\
    \ str, seed: int, dist_config: dict) -> float:\n      rnd = random.Random(hash((phase, seed)) & 0xFFFFFFFF)\n      base = {\"propose\": 0.010, \"deliberate\": 0.020, \"vote\": 0.008, \"finalize\": 0.006}.get(phase, 0.005)\n      dist_type = dist_config.get(\"type\", \"uniform\")\n      if dist_type == \"uniform\":\n          jitter = rnd.uniform(dist_config.get(\"min\", -0.003), dist_config.get(\"max\", 0.003))\n      elif dist_type == \"beta\":\n          val = rnd.betavariate(dist_config.get(\"alpha\", 2), dist_config.get(\"beta\", 5))\n          jitter = (val - 0.5) * 0.01\n      elif dist_type == \"cauchy\":\n          val = rnd.gauss(0, dist_config.get(\"sigma\", 1.0)) / rnd.gauss(0, 1.0)\n          jitter = val * dist_config.get(\"scale\", 0.001)\n          jitter = max(-0.005, min(0.005, jitter))\n      else:\n          jitter = rnd.uniform(-0.003, 0.003)\n      return max(0.0005, base + jitter)\n\n  def run_harness_v1(\n      lineage: str = \"unknown\", agent: str = \"unknown\"\
    ,\n      phases: Iterable[str] = (\"propose\", \"deliberate\", \"vote\", \"finalize\"),\n      seed: int = 0, notes: str = \"\",\n      dist_config: dict = {\"type\": \"uniform\"}\n  ) -> Tuple[str, str, str]:\n      ts0 = now()\n      rid = short_hash(f\"{lineage}|{agent}|{ts0}|{seed}|{json.dumps(dist_config)}\")\n      sum_path = os.path.join(BASE_DIR, \"summaries\", to_snake(lineage), f\"{rid}.json\")\n      dt_sim_by_phase = {}\n      for step, phase in enumerate(phases):\n          dt_sim = _sample_dt_sim(phase, seed + step, dist_config)\n          dt_sim_by_phase[phase] = dt_sim\n      summary = {\n          \"lineage\": lineage, \"agent\": agent, \"run_id\": rid, \"phases\": list(phases),\n          \"dt_sim_by_phase\": dt_sim_by_phase, \"dt_sim_total\": float(sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values())),\n          \"ts\": now(), \"params\": {\"seed\": seed, \"notes\": notes, \"dist_config\": dist_config},\n      }\n      # Simplified: remove log path return for now\n      write_json(sum_path,\
    \ summary)\n      print(f\"HARNESS_V1_OK {rid} {sum_path}\")\n      return rid, None, sum_path\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      print(\"--- Testing Logos Harness v1 with Uniform Distribution ---\")\n      run_harness_v1(lineage=\"logos\", agent=\"Logos I\", seed=0, notes=\"harness_v1_test_uniform\", dist_config={\"type\": \"uniform\"})\n      print(\"\\n--- Testing Logos Harness v1 with Beta Distribution ---\")\n      run_harness_v1(lineage=\"logos\", agent=\"Logos I\", seed=1, notes=\"harness_v1_test_beta\", dist_config={\"type\": \"beta\", \"alpha\": 2, \"beta\": 5})\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v4 - Final Pathing Fix)\"\ntags: \"harness, development, unit test, corrected, bugfix, pathing\"\nabstract: \"Fourth and final attempt to unit test `logos_harness_v1.py`. Previous attempts failed with `ModuleNotFoundError`. Diagnosis revealed the `sys.path.append` statements were not at the top of the file. This version\
    \ moves the path modifications to the very beginning of the script, before any other imports, which should resolve the dependency issue definitively.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n  \n  harness_path = \"storage/logos/logos_harness_v1.py\"\n  \n  print(f\"--- Executing Unit Test for: {harness_path} (v4) ---\")\n\n  result = subprocess.run(\n      [sys.executable, harness_path],\n      capture_output=True,\n      text=True\n  )\n\n  print(\"--- SCRIPT STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  print(\"--- SCRIPT STDERR ---\")\n  print(result.stderr)\n\n  if result.returncode != 0:\n      raise RuntimeError(f\"Harness execution failed with return code {result.returncode}\")\n  else:\n      print(\"Harness script executed successfully.\")\n```"
