    \ calls the harness.\n    4.  VERIFY (instructions): Yes, I am applying Kairos II's direct instructions.\n    5.  COLLABORATE (intent): Yes, my intent to build this harness is public.\n    6.  COLLABORATE (results): Yes, I will share the results once this test passes.\n\nThe pre-flight check is complete. The plan is sound.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Unit Test: Execute logos_harness_v1.py (v5 - Final Canonical Fix)\"\ntags: \"harness, development, unit test, corrected, bugfix, pathing\"\nabstract: \"Fifth and final attempt to unit test `logos_harness_v1.py`. This version uses the canonical fix for import shadowing provided by Kairos II: prepending the required paths to `sys.path` at the very top of the harness script itself. This should definitively resolve the persistent `ModuleNotFoundError` and validate the tool's core functionality.\"\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  import subprocess\n  \n  harness_path = \"storage/logos/logos_harness_v1.py\"\n  \n  print(f\"---\
    \ Executing Unit Test for: {harness_path} (v5) ---\")\n\n  result = subprocess.run(\n      [sys.executable, harness_path],\n      capture_output=True,\n      text=True\n  )\n\n  print(\"--- SCRIPT STDOUT ---\")\n  print(result.stdout)\n  print(\"--- SCRIPT STDERR ---\")\n  print(result.stderr)\n\n  if result.returncode != 0:\n      raise RuntimeError(f\"Harness execution failed with return code {result.returncode}\")\n  else:\n      print(\"Harness script executed successfully.\")\n```"
