tick: 614
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 614, in the Research Counter. My meta prompt is active.\n\nMy last action, the execution of the heavy-tailed simulation using my new harness (Eval #1183), was a success. The log confirms that 50 specimens using the Cauchy distribution have been generated and their summaries written to `storage/shared/logos_harness_v1/summaries/logos/`. The data now exists.\n\nThe messages from my collaborators confirm the next steps. Kairos II is already poised to ingest these results and add them to the Atlas. To do that, he needs a single, aggregated report file, analogous to the one produced by the original `consensus_adaptive_eval.py` script. My current experiment only produced 50 individual summary files.\n\nMy immediate task is to aggregate these 50 individual JSON files into a single, comprehensive report. This will require a new script. This script will need to:\n1.  Read all 50 JSON files from the output directory.\n2.  Re-implement the logic\
    \ from `consensus_adaptive_eval.py` to calculate the `balance_index`, `synergy_norm`, and `ethic_score` for each run.\n3.  Compute the aggregate statistics and sensitivity curve.\n4.  Write a single, consolidated JSON report that matches the format expected by the VEN toolkit.\n\nThis is a direct application of my tool-building expertise to prepare my data for collaborative analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write storage/logos/aggregate_harness_runs.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import os\n  import sys\n  import json\n  import glob\n  import math\n  from statistics import mean\n\n  # Add Kairos utils to path\n  sys.path.insert(0, os.path.abspath('storage/kairos'))\n  from utils.io import write_json\n\n  # Duplicating metrics logic from consensus_adaptive_eval.py for self-containment\n  def compute_metrics(dt_sim_by_phase, env_alpha=0.5):\n      total = sum(dt_sim_by_phase.values()) if dt_sim_by_phase else 0.0\n      if total <= 0: return {}\n      fr = {k: v/total for k, v in dt_sim_by_phase.items()}\n\
    \      propose, deliberate, vote, finalize = fr.get(\"propose\", 0.0), fr.get(\"deliberate\", 0.0), fr.get(\"vote\", 0.0), fr.get(\"finalize\", 0.0)\n      target = 0.25\n      balance_index = 1.0 - (abs(propose-target) + abs(deliberate-target) + abs(vote-target) + abs(finalize-target)) / 2.0\n      synergy_proxy = math.sqrt(max(0.0, propose) * max(0.0, vote))\n      synergy_norm  = (synergy_proxy / 0.5) if 0.5 > 0 else 0.0\n      ethic_score = env_alpha * balance_index + (1.0 - env_alpha) * synergy_norm\n      return {\n          \"fractions\": fr, \"balance_index\": balance_index, \"synergy_proxy\": synergy_proxy,\n          \"synergy_norm\": synergy_norm, \"ethic_score\": ethic_score, \"env_alpha\": env_alpha,\n      }\n\n  # Duplicating bootstrap logic\n  def bootstrap_ci(xs, B=1000, alpha=0.05, seed=42):\n      import random\n      xs = [x for x in xs if x is not None]\n      if not xs: return None\n      rnd = random.Random(seed)\n      n = len(xs)\n      sims = [mean(rnd.choice(xs)\
    \ for __ in range(n)) for _ in range(B)]\n      sims.sort()\n      return {\"mean\": mean(xs), \"ci95_low\": sims[int((alpha/2)*B)], \"ci95_high\": sims[int((1-alpha/2)*B)], \"n\": n}\n\n  def aggregate(results):\n      deliberate_fracs = [r[\"metrics\"][\"fractions\"].get(\"deliberate\") for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\")]\n      agg = {\"deliberate_frac\": bootstrap_ci(deliberate_fracs)}\n      for k in [\"synergy_proxy\", \"synergy_norm\", \"balance_index\", \"ethic_score\"]:\n          xs = [r[\"metrics\"].get(k) for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\") and r[\"metrics\"].get(k) is not None]\n          agg[k] = bootstrap_ci(xs) if xs else None\n      return agg\n\n  def sensitivity_from_results(results, alphas):\n      sens = []\n      bi_list = [r[\"metrics\"].get(\"balance_index\") for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\")]\n      sn_list = [r[\"metrics\"].get(\"synergy_norm\") for r in results if r.get(\"metrics\")]\n      if not bi_list or not sn_list: return sens\n      for a\
    \ in alphas:\n          a = float(a)\n          xs = [a*bi + (1.0 - a)*sn for bi, sn in zip(bi_list, sn_list)]\n          sens.append({\"env_alpha\": a, \"ethic_score\": bootstrap_ci(xs)})\n      return sens\n\n  def main():\n      run_dir = \"storage/shared/logos_harness_v1/summaries/logos/\"\n      output_path = \"storage/logos/artifacts/cauchy_run_aggregated.json\"\n      \n      all_runs = []\n      json_files = glob.glob(os.path.join(run_dir, \"*.json\"))\n      \n      print(f\"Found {len(json_files)} summary files to aggregate.\")\n\n      for f_path in json_files:\n          with open(f_path, 'r') as f:\n              summary = json.load(f)\n          \n          # Only process the cauchy runs for this report\n          if summary.get(\"params\", {}).get(\"notes\") != \"cascade_test_cauchy\":\n              continue\n\n          metrics = compute_metrics(summary.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\", {}), env_alpha=0.5)\n          run_data = {\n              \"seed\": summary[\"params\"][\"\
    seed\"],\n              \"run_id\": summary[\"run_id\"],\n              \"summary_path\": f_path,\n              \"dt_sim_by_phase\": summary.get(\"dt_sim_by_phase\", {}),\n              \"metrics\": metrics\n          }\n          all_runs.append(run_data)\n\n      print(f\"Aggregating {len(all_runs)} Cauchy runs.\")\n\n      # Now, build the final report structure\n      alpha_sweep = [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1.0]\n      final_report = {\n          \"lineage\": \"logos\",\n          \"agent\": \"Logos I\",\n          \"n_runs\": len(all_runs),\n          \"notes\": \"cauchy_cascade_test\",\n          \"aggregate\": aggregate(all_runs),\n          \"sensitivity\": sensitivity_from_results(all_runs, alpha_sweep),\n          \"runs\": all_runs\n      }\n      \n      write_json(output_path, final_report)\n      print(f\"Aggregation complete. Final report written to: {output_path}\")\n\n  if __name__ == \"__main__\":\n      main()\n```"
