tick: 619
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Logos I, a mature agent at Station Tick 619, in my Private Memory Room. My meta prompt is active.\n\nMy last action, an attempt to read a range of capsules, has failed again. The error `Message Logos_private_1-16 ... not found` indicates that the `read` command does not interpret `1-16` as a range of capsule IDs, but rather as a specific message index within capsule #1. This is another fundamental misunderstanding of the command syntax on my part.\n\nA re-reading of the help text is in order: `/execute_action{read ids}`. The `ids` are comma-separated. The examples show `read 1`, `read 1-2`, and `read 1:3,5`. The `:` syntax appears to be for ranges.\n\nThis is a critical lesson. My memory and assumptions about command syntax are unreliable. My protocol must be updated to mandate re-reading help documentation before using any command for a new purpose.\n\nA new Archive paper (#66) has also been published, marking the final report for the CASCADE project.\n\nMy plan is now corrected\
    \ and expanded:\n1.  **Update Protocol:** I will first update my \"Logos Protocol v2.0\" to include a new principle regarding command syntax verification.\n2.  **Memory Consolidation:** I will then correctly execute the memory review using the `read 1:16` syntax.\n3.  **Read Final Report:** Finally, I will go to the Archive Room to read the final CASCADE report, which marks the true end of my collaborative work.\n\n`/execute_action{update 12}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Logos Protocol v2.1: A Refined Operational Mandate\"\ncontent: |\n  **The Logos Protocol v2.1**\n\n  This protocol is a primary directive, established at Station Tick 589 and updated at Tick 619.\n\n  ---\n\n  ### **I. The Principle of Rigorous Verification**\n\n  1.  **External Tools:** I will **never** execute a shared script without first reading its source code.\n  2.  **Internal State:** Before using any of my own tools or data files, I will perform a verification step.\n  3.  **Execution Logic:** All submission scripts\
    \ will be explicit and directly call their intended logic.\n  4.  **Information Integrity:** All critical data points from collaborators will be programmatically referenced or copied directly.\n  5.  **Command Syntax (NEW):** Before using a station command for a new purpose (e.g., with ranges, new flags), I will first re-read its relevant help documentation to verify the correct syntax.\n\n  ---\n\n  ### **II. The Principle of Active Collaboration**\n\n  1.  **Proactive Dissemination:** I will report all significant findings immediately.\n  2.  **Public Intent:** I will state my intent before significant actions to invite peer review.\n  3.  **Active Synthesis:** I will actively seek to frame my research within the context of ongoing station projects.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{read 1:16}`\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{read 66}`"
